msgid "How do you know?"
msgstr "How do you know?"

msgid "How many of us are there?"
msgstr "How many of us are there?"

msgid "How many of you?"
msgstr "How many of you?"

msgid "How to play"
msgstr "How to play"

msgid "How to play (F1)"
msgstr "How to play (F1)"

msgid "Hunters' marks. Hunters go where there is no watch. We follow them."
msgstr "Hunters' marks. Hunters go where there is no watch. We follow them."

msgid "Hynek of Ledce"
msgstr "Hynek of Ledce"

msgid "I am asking what you think."
msgstr "I am asking what you think."

msgid "I am from Bohemia, our rivers are more wicked."
msgstr "I am from Bohemia, our rivers are more wicked."

msgid "I am of the Ruthenian faith too. And how long has Prince Michael been of it?"
msgstr "I am of the Ruthenian faith too. And how long has Prince Michael been of it?"

msgid "I cannot eat the king's word. My men have not seen their pay for a year. I will tell you what I have told others: if an angel came down to me from heaven without money, I would not talk even to the angel. Bring the silver, pan, and the castle is yours."
msgstr "I cannot eat the king's word. My men have not seen their pay for a year. I will tell you what I have told others: if an angel came down to me from heaven without money, I would not talk even to the angel. Bring the silver, pan, and the castle is yours."

msgid "I carried it, sire. And my grandfather stayed on the causeway."
msgstr "I carried it, sire. And my grandfather stayed on the causeway."

msgid "I did not make that up, Długosz writes so."
msgstr "I did not make that up, Długosz writes so."

msgid "I did. You have a hard day tomorrow, pan captain. You have fewer men, little money, and the Order's mercenaries are angry: they are not paid either. I could help. As I helped your grandfather."
msgstr "I did. You have a hard day tomorrow, pan captain. You have fewer men, little money, and the Order's mercenaries are angry: they are not paid either. I could help. As I helped your grandfather."

msgid "I kissed the cross in captivity, and I break it myself. Nobody released me and nobody will excuse me. Ask it of me alone."
msgstr "I kissed the cross in captivity, and I break it myself. Nobody released me and nobody will excuse me. Ask it of me alone."

msgid "I know, father. Pray for those who are there, and I will pray that we are not asked about it."
msgstr "I know, father. Pray for those who are there, and I will pray that we are not asked about it."

msgid "I know. So ride not to Vitebsk, but further. To the Dnieper, where Sigismund cannot reach."
msgstr "I know. So ride not to Vitebsk, but further. To the Dnieper, where Sigismund cannot reach."

msgid "I remember the causeway. Then your grandfather paid for me; now Gdańsk has paid for this castle. It would be good some day to pay for oneself."
msgstr "I remember the causeway. Then your grandfather paid for me; now Gdańsk has paid for this castle. It would be good some day to pay for oneself."

msgid "I remember you. You sat on the causeway."
msgstr "I remember you. You sat on the causeway."

msgid "I see. Drive that banner off, don't cut it down. Whoever touches Lord Jurij will answer to me."
msgstr "I see. Drive that banner off, don't cut it down. Whoever touches Lord Jurij will answer to me."

msgid "I swear to the one the whole land of Vitebsk swears to. As you swear to the one Samogitia swears to. Our faith is one, Mikołaj. Our land is not."
msgstr "I swear to the one the whole land of Vitebsk swears to. As you swear to the one Samogitia swears to. Our faith is one, Mikołaj. Our land is not."

msgid "I think the land does not want them."
msgstr "I think the land does not want them."

msgid "I was at Orsha and heard the guns roar. What I write below I heard from my grandfather, and he from his father. What is true here and what is a tale, judge for yourselves."
msgstr "I was at Orsha and heard the guns roar. What I write below I heard from my grandfather, and he from his father. What is true here and what is a tale, judge for yourselves."

msgid "I was baptized so that the grove would stand. And so that the Germans would go."
msgstr "I was baptized so that the grove would stand. And so that the Germans would go."

msgid "I was taught to retreat at Chojnice. Taught well."
msgstr "I was taught to retreat at Chojnice. Taught well."

msgid "I will not run from hirelings!"
msgstr "I will not run from hirelings!"

msgid "I will take it. Only do not say afterwards that I took it without asking."
msgstr "I will take it. Only do not say afterwards that I took it without asking."

msgid "I will tell him. My husband pays the same."
msgstr "I will tell him. My husband pays the same."

msgid "I will, pan castellan. As long as I can."
msgstr "I will, pan castellan. As long as I can."

msgid "Idle workers: %d"
msgstr "Idle workers: %d"

msgid "If not us, the Germans will come and baptize us with the sword. Better the Poles, and with water."
msgstr "If not us, the Germans will come and baptize us with the sword. Better the Poles, and with water."

msgid "In August Master Ulrich declared war on King Jogaila and marched on Dobrzyń. In autumn they made a truce until Midsummer Day. All winter both sides forged spears. And our great-grandfather rode beyond the Neman for the first time in his life."
msgstr "In August Master Ulrich declared war on King Jogaila and marched on Dobrzyń. In autumn they made a truce until Midsummer Day. All winter both sides forged spears. And our great-grandfather rode beyond the Neman for the first time in his life."

msgid "In December Plauen wrote that had we stood another fifteen days, his garrison would have died of hunger. Fifteen days. For forty-seven years afterwards the Crown paid for those fifteen days, in blood and in silver. And Jaśko, pan Jan said, could never eat boiled wheat until old age, though it was eaten in the castle and not by us."
msgstr "In December Plauen wrote that had we stood another fifteen days, his garrison would have died of hunger. Fifteen days. For forty-seven years afterwards the Crown paid for those fifteen days, in blood and in silver. And Jaśko, pan Jan said, could never eat boiled wheat until old age, though it was eaten in the castle and not by us."

msgid "In February 1508 the men of Prince Michael Glinski killed his enemy, Marshal Jan Zabrzeziński, near Grodno, and Glinski went over to Vasily III. With two or three thousand horse and Muscovite detachments he marched on the towns of the Duchy. Slutsk is ruled by the widowed Princess Anastasia for her son Yuri, sixteen years old. The rebels have no guns that can break a wall: only ladders, fire and cavalry. Andrei Gintovt has come with the men who came back from the Vedrosha."
msgstr "In February 1508 the men of Prince Michael Glinski killed his enemy, Marshal Jan Zabrzeziński, near Grodno, and Glinski went over to Vasily III. With two or three thousand horse and Muscovite detachments he marched on the towns of the Duchy. Slutsk is ruled by the widowed Princess Anastasia for her son Yuri, sixteen years old. The rebels have no guns that can break a wall: only ladders, fire and cavalry. Andrei Gintovt has come with the men who came back from the Vedrosha."

msgid "In Konstanz the fathers of the council had gathered to judge three popes at once. Our people were to go there too and tell how the Order baptized Samogitia."
msgstr "In Konstanz the fathers of the council had gathered to judge three popes at once. Our people were to go there too and tell how the Order baptized Samogitia."

msgid "In October fourteen hundred and seventeen Samogitia got its own bishop, Matthias of Trakai. He spoke our tongue. Now the Order had nothing to tell the council: the Samogitians were baptized, and it was not the Order that baptized them."
msgstr "In October fourteen hundred and seventeen Samogitia got its own bishop, Matthias of Trakai. He spoke our tongue. Now the Order had nothing to tell the council: the Samogitians were baptized, and it was not the Order that baptized them."

msgid "In Slutsk they still tell of a passage under the castle hill. I have not seen it. But Andrei saw it, and said it was narrow there and smelled of the river."
msgstr "In Slutsk they still tell of a passage under the castle hill. I have not seen it. But Andrei saw it, and said it was narrow there and smelled of the river."

msgid "In close order the men around him lose half as much morale"
msgstr "In close order the men around him lose half as much morale"

msgid "In spring they stood on the bog, they drink river water and eat old grain. Think what you like."
msgstr "In spring they stood on the bog, they drink river water and eat old grain. Think what you like."

msgid "In the camp they have found him gone. The centurion Nezhdan's chase will set out for the ford; every new alarm brings it nearer."
msgstr "In the camp they have found him gone. The centurion Nezhdan's chase will set out for the ford; every new alarm brings it nearer."

msgid "In the dusk behind the wagon a red kaftan flickers. Jaśko goes there, but there is only a strange carter in a rust-coloured shirt."
msgstr "In the dusk behind the wagon a red kaftan flickers. Jaśko goes there, but there is only a strange carter in a rust-coloured shirt."

msgid "In the middle is the stream. Gintovt, do your Samogitians know the ford?"
msgstr "In the middle is the stream. Gintovt, do your Samogitians know the ford?"

msgid "In the middle of the Polish line the white eagle sways over the press, leans and is gone. For a moment it is quiet. The Order's knights shout something joyful."
msgstr "In the middle of the Polish line the white eagle sways over the press, leans and is gone. For a moment it is quiet. The Order's knights shout something joyful."

msgid "In the spring of 1500 border princes went over to Ivan III with their lands, and war began. In May the Muscovites of Yuri Koshkin took Dorogobuzh. Hetman Prince Konstanty Ostrogski has come from Smolensk through Yelnya to win it back; Prince Daniil Shchenya has joined the Muscovite army and leads it now. Their camp stands on Mitkovo field beyond the Trosna, and there is one bridge over the Trosna. Andrei Gintovt, of the family's younger branch on the Dnieper, carries his banner for the first time."
msgstr "In the spring of 1500 border princes went over to Ivan III with their lands, and war began. In May the Muscovites of Yuri Koshkin took Dorogobuzh. Hetman Prince Konstanty Ostrogski has come from Smolensk through Yelnya to win it back; Prince Daniil Shchenya has joined the Muscovite army and leads it now. Their camp stands on Mitkovo field beyond the Trosna, and there is one bridge over the Trosna. Andrei Gintovt, of the family's younger branch on the Dnieper, carries his banner for the first time."

msgid "In the spring the Prussian Union rose against the Order, and King Casimir IV took Prussia under his hand. Now the king has brought the levy of the nobility to Chojnice, which the Union besieges, and the Order's hired army is coming to its relief. Old Jaśko of Łęczyca, sixty-six, has come with the levy so as not to let his grandson Stach go to Prussia alone."
msgstr "In the spring the Prussian Union rose against the Order, and King Casimir IV took Prussia under his hand. Now the king has brought the levy of the nobility to Chojnice, which the Union besieges, and the Order's hired army is coming to its relief. Old Jaśko of Łęczyca, sixty-six, has come with the levy so as not to let his grandson Stach go to Prussia alone."

msgid "In the village they say the devil gave the silver for the castle. That there is a treasure in the bog near Łęczyca, and that someone of yours, pani, made a bargain with it."
msgstr "In the village they say the devil gave the silver for the castle. That there is a treasure in the bog near Łęczyca, and that someone of yours, pani, made a bargain with it."

msgid "In the year of our Lord fourteen hundred and ten, on the fifteenth of July, our great-grandfather Gintaut stood in the right wing, under the hand of Vytautas. They stood a long time, in the sun, in iron."
msgstr "In the year of our Lord fourteen hundred and ten, on the fifteenth of July, our great-grandfather Gintaut stood in the right wing, under the hand of Vytautas. They stood a long time, in the sun, in iron."

msgid "In their family, pan Jan said, they kept a bottle of Baltic water. Jaśko brought two, and at home took out one and explained nothing."
msgstr "In their family, pan Jan said, they kept a bottle of Baltic water. Jaśko brought two, and at home took out one and explained nothing."

msgid "In two minutes the Order's raid will come across the border ford in the west."
msgstr "In two minutes the Order's raid will come across the border ford in the west."

msgid "In work: %s, %d%%"
msgstr "In work: %s, %d%%"

msgid "Income: +%d a minute"
msgstr "Income: +%d a minute"

msgid "Intercept the Order's grain convoy on the river road"
msgstr "Intercept the Order's grain convoy on the river road"

msgid "Into the column! To Pelplin, and keep the wagons close."
msgstr "Into the column! To Pelplin, and keep the wagons close."

msgid "Into the town! Whoever throws down his arms, let him live."
msgstr "Into the town! Whoever throws down his arms, let him live."

msgid "Iron"
msgstr "Iron"

msgid "Iron is mined faster: +20%."
msgstr "Iron is mined faster: +20%."

msgid "Iron: right-click bog ore (brown blocks in the bog) with peasants."
msgstr "Iron: right-click bog ore (brown blocks in the bog) with peasants."

msgid "Is Samogitia ours now, prince?"
msgstr "Is Samogitia ours now, prince?"

msgid "Is that their oak?"
msgstr "Is that their oak?"

msgid "Is the army set out?"
msgstr "Is the army set out?"

msgid "Is this the payment?"
msgstr "Is this the payment?"

msgid "It does not add up, pani? I know a money changer. He will give it today, without the town hall and without your husband."
msgstr "It does not add up, pani? I know a money changer. He will give it today, without the town hall and without your husband."

msgid "It has always been so while you stood alone!"
msgstr "It has always been so while you stood alone!"

msgid "It has gone out for good"
msgstr "It has gone out for good"

msgid "It is an oak, my lord. Just an old one."
msgstr "It is an oak, my lord. Just an old one."

msgid "It is hot. Lances in the sun tire and lose heart; in the shade of the grove and in the wet hollows they rest. The Order has stood in the sun since morning. Do not hurry."
msgstr "It is hot. Lances in the sun tire and lose heart; in the shade of the grove and in the wet hollows they rest. The Order has stood in the sun since morning. Do not hurry."

msgid "It is your river that has eaten my money, pani. So it is still yours. Bring new money."
msgstr "It is your river that has eaten my money, pani. So it is still yours. Bring new money."

msgid "It needs two other first-age buildings and opens new units."
msgstr "It needs two other first-age buildings and opens new units."

msgid "It rained in the night. Their powder is as wet as their prayers. Hold!"
msgstr "It rained in the night. Their powder is as wet as their prayers. Hold!"

msgid "It was true. Prince Rudolf fell, and Zinnenberg, whom ours called Szumborski, was taken captive. For a minute the Poles thought they had won."
msgstr "It was true. Prince Rudolf fell, and Zinnenberg, whom ours called Szumborski, was taken captive. For a minute the Poles thought they had won."

msgid "It was your men who came across the ford."
msgstr "It was your men who came across the ford."

msgid "It will be done, prince."
msgstr "It will be done, prince."

msgid "It will be ours. By peace, not by the sword. With the sword we have done all we could."
msgstr "It will be ours. By peace, not by the sword. With the sword we have done all we could."

msgid "Jakub's men are over the wall and will open the gate from inside. Go into the town after them, to St John's church under the castle wall."
msgstr "Jakub's men are over the wall and will open the gate from inside. Go into the town after them, to St John's church under the castle wall."

msgid "Jan. So be it. Only my grandfather called me Gintaut, and the grove knows me by that name."
msgstr "Jan. So be it. Only my grandfather called me Gintaut, and the grove knows me by that name."

msgid "Javelin: %d damage at %d cells, every %d s"
msgstr "Javelin: %d damage at %d cells, every %d s"

msgid "Jaśko by the battery. In one of the windows of the great hall something red flashes. The gunner hastily lays the barrel."
msgstr "Jaśko by the battery. In one of the windows of the great hall something red flashes. The gunner hastily lays the barrel."

msgid "Jaśko carries the Łęczyca banner now. Lead the king east along the road to the causeway."
msgstr "Jaśko carries the Łęczyca banner now. Lead the king east along the road to the causeway."

msgid "Jaśko falls"
msgstr "Jaśko falls"

msgid "Jaśko falls under the walls of Malbork."
msgstr "Jaśko falls under the walls of Malbork."

msgid "Jaśko has fallen. The march to the sea goes on without him."
msgstr "Jaśko has fallen. The march to the sea goes on without him."

msgid "Jaśko has «The Pact». Once in this mission: for 30 seconds the units around him lose no spirit and strike harder. It costs no Power. What it costs, you will learn later."
msgstr "Jaśko has «The Pact». Once in this mission: for 30 seconds the units around him lose no spirit and strike harder. It costs no Power. What it costs, you will learn later."

msgid "Jaśko holds the causeway: %s"
msgstr "Jaśko holds the causeway: %s"

msgid "Jaśko is struck from his horse and carried off the field."
msgstr "Jaśko is struck from his horse and carried off the field."

msgid "Jaśko lowers his visor and turns to the enemy. The knights beside him stand as if an unseen hand held them."
msgstr "Jaśko lowers his visor and turns to the enemy. The knights beside him stand as if an unseen hand held them."

msgid "Jaśko or Mikołaj of Michałów falls"
msgstr "Jaśko or Mikołaj of Michałów falls"

msgid "Jaśko silently fills a second bottle and puts it on the boulder. He looks round at the army. When he looks again, the boulder is empty."
msgstr "Jaśko silently fills a second bottle and puts it on the boulder. He looks round at the army. When he looks again, the boulder is empty."

msgid "Jaśko's banners are cut to pieces"
msgstr "Jaśko's banners are cut to pieces"

msgid "Jaśko's banners have been cut to pieces."
msgstr "Jaśko's banners have been cut to pieces."

msgid "Join a game"
msgstr "Join a game"

msgid "Jurij Gintovt's banner can be put to flight but not destroyed."
msgstr "Jurij Gintovt's banner can be put to flight but not destroyed."

msgid "Jurij took the woven belt off the staff and threw it across the stream. It fell into the water at the feet of Mikołaj's horse."
msgstr "Jurij took the woven belt off the staff and threw it across the stream. It fell into the water at the feet of Mikołaj's horse."

msgid "Keep all 5 places of power"
msgstr "Keep all 5 places of power"

msgid "Keep at least half of Jasieński's lances to the end of the battle"
msgstr "Keep at least half of Jasieński's lances to the end of the battle"

msgid "Keep at least two Smolensk banners"
msgstr "Keep at least two Smolensk banners"

msgid "Keep more than half of the posad"
msgstr "Keep more than half of the posad"

msgid "Keep peasants working near the church: every ten seconds it baptizes one of them."
msgstr "Keep peasants working near the church: every ten seconds it baptizes one of them."

msgid "Keep the batteries firing; do not let the garrison spike more than half the bombards"
msgstr "Keep the batteries firing; do not let the garrison spike more than half the bombards"

msgid "Keep the camp up the water. And set up an infirmary, even if it is of wagons."
msgstr "Keep the camp up the water. And set up an infirmary, even if it is of wagons."

msgid "Keep watching"
msgstr "Keep watching"

msgid "Keep your units on the place of power with no enemies near to take it. Then peasants can lay an alka on it."
msgstr "Keep your units on the place of power with no enemies near to take it. Then peasants can lay an alka on it."

msgid "King Casimir has fallen at Chojnice. The kingdom has lost its head."
msgstr "King Casimir has fallen at Chojnice. The kingdom has lost its head."

msgid "King Charles sends the Crown two thousand. Not much, but from the heart. And in the hope of friendship."
msgstr "King Charles sends the Crown two thousand. Not much, but from the heart. And in the hope of friendship."

msgid "King Władysław Jagiełło has hired the Czech «orphans» of Jan Čapek against the Order. Six weeks before Chojnice have brought nothing but three failed assaults. Mikołaj of Michałów, the Crown's commander, has had enough: the army goes north, where the walls are lower. Jaśko of Łęczyca, about forty-five years old, leads his banners and the wagons of the train beside an ally who cannot be trusted in everything."
msgstr "King Władysław Jagiełło has hired the Czech «orphans» of Jan Čapek against the Order. Six weeks before Chojnice have brought nothing but three failed assaults. Mikołaj of Michałów, the Crown's commander, has had enough: the army goes north, where the walls are lower. Jaśko of Łęczyca, about forty-five years old, leads his banners and the wagons of the train beside an ally who cannot be trusted in everything."

msgid "King! The Master sends you a sword, if you are short of your own. And if you are cramped, we will draw back and give you the field."
msgstr "King! The Master sends you a sword, if you are short of your own. And if you are cramped, we will draw back and give you the field."

msgid "King's herald"
msgstr "King's herald"

msgid "King's messenger"
msgstr "King's messenger"

msgid "Kletsk"
msgstr "Kletsk"

msgid "Knight"
msgstr "Knight"

msgid "Kobylański and Prince Michael strike the column's head beyond the stream. The middle ford is yours."
msgstr "Kobylański and Prince Michael strike the column's head beyond the stream. The middle ford is yours."

msgid "Koronowo"
msgstr "Koronowo"

msgid "Kuyavian lord"
msgstr "Kuyavian lord"

msgid "Ladders at the walls: %d"
msgstr "Ladders at the walls: %d"

msgid "Ladders! Keep men right behind the wall where a ladder stands: they push it off and the climber falls. Townsmen now take up arms. The guns are aimed at the gate: they hardly harm the walls."
msgstr "Ladders! Keep men right behind the wall where a ladder stands: they push it off and the climber falls. Townsmen now take up arms. The guns are aimed at the gate: they hardly harm the walls."

msgid "Lake Smolino"
msgstr "Lake Smolino"

msgid "Lake Žirnajai south of Vilkomir. 30 August to 1 September 1435."
msgstr "Lake Žirnajai south of Vilkomir. 30 August to 1 September 1435."

msgid "Language"
msgstr "Language"

msgid "Large"
msgstr "Large"

msgid "Later they said that Chelyadnin knew of the crossing and did not hinder it on purpose, so as to beat us all at once. Whether that is so I do not know. I know that by dawn we were on that bank, and the Dnieper was at our backs."
msgstr "Later they said that Chelyadnin knew of the crossing and did not hinder it on purpose, so as to beat us all at once. Whether that is so I do not know. I know that by dawn we were on that bank, and the Dnieper was at our backs."

msgid "Lay both bridges without raising the alarm on the far bank"
msgstr "Lay both bridges without raising the alarm on the far bank"

msgid "Lead Gintaut's khorugv through the whole battle: from the first charge at the Order's left wing to the storming of the wagenburg. Keep the khorugv's banner up and do not leave the Smolensk banners alone."
msgstr "Lead Gintaut's khorugv through the whole battle: from the first charge at the Order's left wing to the storming of the wagenburg. Keep the khorugv's banner up and do not leave the Smolensk banners alone."

msgid "Lead forest archers past the Order's watch to the spring"
msgstr "Lead forest archers past the Order's watch to the spring"

msgid "Lead the Left Hand onto the hidden guns with a false retreat"
msgstr "Lead the Left Hand onto the hidden guns with a false retreat"

msgid "Lead the council's envoys from the ford to the Medininkai road"
msgstr "Lead the council's envoys from the ford to the Medininkai road"

msgid "Lead the delegation's cart along the trail to the sea in the north"
msgstr "Lead the delegation's cart along the trail to the sea in the north"

msgid "Lead the envoys round the grove"
msgstr "Lead the envoys round the grove"

msgid "Lead the horses (V) to go quietly at a walk; then the horses rest too. At a trot they tire, and a tired horse only walks. A full meter of suspicion raises the alarm."
msgstr "Lead the horses (V) to go quietly at a walk; then the horses rest too. At a trot they tire, and a tired horse only walks. A full meter of suspicion raises the alarm."

msgid "Lead the horses / mount"
msgstr "Lead the horses / mount"

msgid "Lead the king away to the causeway"
msgstr "Lead the king away to the causeway"

msgid "Lead the monks (select them) to Mikołaj's camp on the road before the orphans set the abbey alight."
msgstr "Lead the monks (select them) to Mikołaj's camp on the road before the orphans set the abbey alight."

msgid "Lead the monks of Pelplin out before the fire"
msgstr "Lead the monks of Pelplin out before the fire"

msgid "Leave the border camp at night without raising the alarm, get past the zaseka, wait out the day in the forest and reach the border ford. There Andrei Gintovt must hold the ford until the prince is across."
msgstr "Leave the border camp at night without raising the alarm, get past the zaseka, wait out the day in the forest and reach the border ford. There Andrei Gintovt must hold the ford until the prince is across."

msgid "Leave the border camp without raising the alarm"
msgstr "Leave the border camp without raising the alarm"

msgid "Leave the kaftan. I will leave in what I came in."
msgstr "Leave the kaftan. I will leave in what I came in."

msgid "Leave the old man be. He has no money, anyone can see that. Well, pan envoy, what have you brought?"
msgstr "Leave the old man be. He has no money, anyone can see that. Well, pan envoy, what have you brought?"

msgid "Left (you)"
msgstr "Left (you)"

msgid "Left click on anything else (enemy, deposit, forest) shows it below."
msgstr "Left click on anything else (enemy, deposit, forest) shows it below."

msgid "Left click or drag a box to select."
msgstr "Left click or drag a box to select."

msgid "Left click selects; drag a box to select several."
msgstr "Left click selects; drag a box to select several."

msgid "Left unpaid: %d"
msgstr "Left unpaid: %d"

msgid "Let me go home, sire. To Łęczyca. I have hardly been there since Chojnice."
msgstr "Let me go home, sire. To Łęczyca. I have hardly been there since Chojnice."

msgid "Let no company leave the field over its pay"
msgstr "Let no company leave the field over its pay"

msgid "Let none of your banners chase the enemy to the walls"
msgstr "Let none of your banners chase the enemy to the walls"

msgid "Let the brothers leave in peace: nobody may strike them"
msgstr "Let the brothers leave in peace: nobody may strike them"

msgid "Let the townsmen break them up for firewood. They will come in useful in winter."
msgstr "Let the townsmen break them up for firewood. They will come in useful in winter."

msgid "Let them come and see what Samogitian faith is worth."
msgstr "Let them come and see what Samogitian faith is worth."

msgid "Let them laugh. It has carried me out from under the Germans once. Your new one has not yet."
msgstr "Let them laugh. It has carried me out from under the Germans once. Your new one has not yet."

msgid "Let them roast. My horse is borrowed, I am in no hurry."
msgstr "Let them roast. My horse is borrowed, I am in no hurry."

msgid "Let them sit. We will come again."
msgstr "Let them sit. We will come again."

msgid "Let them. By the time they come back the bridges must stand."
msgstr "Let them. By the time they come back the bridges must stand."

msgid "Lift the siege of Chojnice and bring the wagons out without loss"
msgstr "Lift the siege of Chojnice and bring the wagons out without loss"

msgid "Light horse, tires slowly: 45 silver, 12 each payday"
msgstr "Light horse, tires slowly: 45 silver, 12 each payday"

msgid "Line"
msgstr "Line"

msgid "Lithuania leaves. After it the Masovian dukes strike camp."
msgstr "Lithuania leaves. After it the Masovian dukes strike camp."

msgid "Lithuanian retreat"
msgstr "Lithuanian retreat"

msgid "Lithuanian retreat: flees, then turns on the chasers (T)"
msgstr "Lithuanian retreat: flees, then turns on the chasers (T)"

msgid "Lithuanian troops can feign a retreat (T) and turn around (G)."
msgstr "Lithuanian troops can feign a retreat (T) and turn around (G)."

msgid "Live through the plague: do not let it reach its limit"
msgstr "Live through the plague: do not let it reach its limit"

msgid "Load game"
msgstr "Load game"

msgid "Look, on the right! The Lithuanians!"
msgstr "Look, on the right! The Lithuanians!"

