msgstr "Nezhdan's chase has set out from the camp along the road to the ford."

msgid "Night again. The bog is near: the road goes round it to the south, past the watch."
msgstr "Night again. The bog is near: the road goes round it to the south, past the watch."

msgid "Night by the battery. A campfire. Jaśko is cleaning the barrel of a bombard alone. Out of the dark comes a man in a red kaftan and sits on the gun carriage as on a bench."
msgstr "Night by the battery. A campfire. Jaśko is cleaning the barrel of a bombard alone. Out of the dark comes a man in a red kaftan and sits on the gun carriage as on a bench."

msgid "Night on the first camp. Beyond the fires horses snort, and the Order's riders come out of the dark onto the wagons."
msgstr "Night on the first camp. Beyond the fires horses snort, and the Order's riders come out of the dark onto the wagons."

msgid "Night. A narrow causeway through the bog; along it ride horsemen in a file, men on foot, the king in a ring of knights. Behind, on the causeway, stand Jaśko and a few old knights. The Order's horse comes out of the dark. Beside Jaśko, on the causeway's rail, sits a man in a red caftan who has not aged at all."
msgstr "Night. A narrow causeway through the bog; along it ride horsemen in a file, men on foot, the king in a ring of knights. Behind, on the causeway, stand Jaśko and a few old knights. The Order's horse comes out of the dark. Beside Jaśko, on the causeway's rail, sits a man in a red caftan who has not aged at all."

msgid "Night. The defenders throw beams and stones into the breach. A glow rises over the Nogat: the bridge is burning."
msgstr "Night. The defenders throw beams and stones into the breach. A glow rises over the Nogat: the bridge is burning."

msgid "Night. The edge of the bog. At the start of an old log causeway stands an old herb woman with a lantern and a bunch of herbs at her belt. Far off, dogs are barking. Silently she raises the lantern and points at the causeway: thin poles going out into the quagmire."
msgstr "Night. The edge of the bog. At the start of an old log causeway stands an old herb woman with a lantern and a bunch of herbs at her belt. Far off, dogs are barking. Silently she raises the lantern and points at the causeway: thin poles going out into the quagmire."

msgid "Night. The far bank. Wet men sit by a fire without their horses. Andrei dries the banner. Beyond the river there are torches: they are gathering the captives."
msgstr "Night. The far bank. Wet men sit by a fire without their horses. Andrei dries the banner. Beyond the river there are torches: they are gathering the captives."

