msgstr "Orsha"

msgid "Orsha is won. The campaign of the Grand Duchy is over."
msgstr "Orsha is won. The campaign of the Grand Duchy is over."

msgid "Ostrogski looked across the river, to the ford, where the last of Andrei's riders were coming out on the far bank. Then he gave up his sabre, hilt first. Who exactly took the hetman the Muscovite lists do not say. They say only that he was wounded and was taken to the sovereign in chains."
msgstr "Ostrogski looked across the river, to the ford, where the last of Andrei's riders were coming out on the far bank. Then he gave up his sabre, hilt first. Who exactly took the hetman the Muscovite lists do not say. They say only that he was wounded and was taken to the sovereign in chains."

msgid "Ostrogski rides up onto the bank, wet to the waist. Andrei gets down from his horse."
msgstr "Ostrogski rides up onto the bank, wet to the waist. Andrei gets down from his horse."

msgid "Our great-grandfather Gintaut was neither prince nor lord. A boyar with three farmsteads, one horse and one grove where his grandfathers still prayed. And in the spring of fourteen hundred and nine he decided he would bear it no longer."
msgstr "Our great-grandfather Gintaut was neither prince nor lord. A boyar with three farmsteads, one horse and one grove where his grandfathers still prayed. And in the spring of fourteen hundred and nine he decided he would bear it no longer."

msgid "Our king can borrow. My husband and his town hall will do the counting afterwards."
msgstr "Our king can borrow. My husband and his town hall will do the counting afterwards."

msgid "Our land is not, but our blood is one."
msgstr "Our land is not, but our blood is one."

msgid "Over the Muscovite ranks they raised an icon, and singing came across the field."
msgstr "Over the Muscovite ranks they raised an icon, and singing came across the field."

msgid "Over the bog: %d"
msgstr "Over the bog: %d"

msgid "Over the hills, then, pan Jan. There will be no grove in the report to the council."
msgstr "Over the hills, then, pan Jan. There will be no grove in the report to the council."

msgid "P pauses, Esc or F10 opens the menu, F1 shows this page."
msgstr "P pauses, Esc or F10 opens the menu, F1 shows this page."

msgid "Pagan elder"
msgstr "Pagan elder"

msgid "Pan Dunin, let me begin. My lances have stood too long."
msgstr "Pan Dunin, let me begin. My lances have stood too long."

msgid "Pan Dunin, the Gdańsk men have sent silver. Enough for five companies, not for six."
msgstr "Pan Dunin, the Gdańsk men have sent silver. Enough for five companies, not for six."

msgid "Pan Jan loved this place. He said that everyone whispered of the devil's silver, but the real silver was from Gdańsk, borrowed, and the town paid that debt off for many years afterwards. There were no devils in it, there were merchants."
msgstr "Pan Jan loved this place. He said that everyone whispered of the devil's silver, but the real silver was from Gdańsk, borrowed, and the town paid that debt off for many years afterwards. There were no devils in it, there were merchants."

msgid "Pan Jan never knew whether the king was right or not. I do not know either. I know that by morning there was no breach, and no bridge either."
msgstr "Pan Jan never knew whether the king was right or not. I do not know either. I know that by morning there was no breach, and no bridge either."

msgid "Pan Jan of Łęczyca told me at Orsha about his great-grandfather Jaśko. That day Jaśko was twenty-two years old, the armour on him was another man's, and his horse was borrowed. Ours stood in the grove, the Germans stood in the sun, and the king was still hearing Mass."
msgstr "Pan Jan of Łęczyca told me at Orsha about his great-grandfather Jaśko. That day Jaśko was twenty-two years old, the armour on him was another man's, and his horse was borrowed. Ours stood in the grove, the Germans stood in the sun, and the king was still hearing Mass."

msgid "Pan Jan said his father told of that night only in his old age. And added that it might have been just a sutler who wanted to sell him wine on credit. There were plenty of them in the camp."
msgstr "Pan Jan said his father told of that night only in his old age. And added that it might have been just a sutler who wanted to sell him wine on credit. There were plenty of them in the camp."

msgid "Pan Jan said that his father Stach was nineteen then, and his father's grandfather Jaśko sixty-six. Jaśko did not have to go: he had done his fighting. But when the levy was called, he said he would not let his grandson go to Prussia alone."
msgstr "Pan Jan said that his father Stach was nineteen then, and his father's grandfather Jaśko sixty-six. Jaśko did not have to go: he had done his fighting. But when the levy was called, he said he would not let his grandson go to Prussia alone."

msgid "Pan Jan's aunt maintained to her old age that it was an ordinary usurer, the Artus Court had a dozen of them of an evening. Maybe. And a day later a man came to her from King Charles of Sweden, who sat in Gdańsk himself then, driven out of his kingdom."
msgstr "Pan Jan's aunt maintained to her old age that it was an ordinary usurer, the Artus Court had a dozen of them of an evening. Maybe. And a day later a man came to her from King Charles of Sweden, who sat in Gdańsk himself then, driven out of his kingdom."

msgid "Pan Jaśko! The orphans have thrown down our chapel. Nobody of ours was by it."
msgstr "Pan Jaśko! The orphans have thrown down our chapel. Nobody of ours was by it."

msgid "Pan Jaśko, there is no more room in my tent. The men drink water from the canal below the place where the horses are watered."
msgstr "Pan Jaśko, there is no more room in my tent. The men drink water from the canal below the place where the horses are watered."

msgid "Pan Jaśko, you stood by this banner when I was not yet in the world. Stand by it now."
msgstr "Pan Jaśko, you stood by this banner when I was not yet in the world. Stand by it now."

msgid "Pan commander, my men have walked barefoot all the way from Bohemia. The king promised boots and twelve groats. I see four hundred pairs of boots, and I have six thousand men."
msgstr "Pan commander, my men have walked barefoot all the way from Bohemia. The king promised boots and twelve groats. I see four hundred pairs of boots, and I have six thousand men."

msgid "Pane, we are hirelings, just like them! We were paid, we served!"
msgstr "Pane, we are hirelings, just like them! We were paid, we served!"

msgid "Pani Barbara is dead. Nobody is left who knows the accounts."
msgstr "Pani Barbara is dead. Nobody is left who knows the accounts."

msgid "Pani Barbara, the peasants of the Żuławy have already come to the town hall. They say they have paid for three wars at once this year."
msgstr "Pani Barbara, the peasants of the Żuławy have already come to the town hall. They say they have paid for three wars at once this year."

