msgid "Seven years after the Vedrosha, Prince Konstanty Ostrogski, the hetman taken captive there, still lives in Muscovy: first in chains, then in honour. In October 1506, after the death of Ivan III, he swore loyal service to Vasily III and received the rank of voivode and lands. In the summer of 1507 he was sent to the border, and there is war between Moscow and Lithuania. Where he slipped away and who rode with him, the sources do not say: this road is the game's."
msgstr "Seven years after the Vedrosha, Prince Konstanty Ostrogski, the hetman taken captive there, still lives in Muscovy: first in chains, then in honour. In October 1506, after the death of Ivan III, he swore loyal service to Vasily III and received the rank of voivode and lands. In the summer of 1507 he was sent to the border, and there is war between Moscow and Lithuania. Where he slipped away and who rode with him, the sources do not say: this road is the game's."

