msgstr "Stop the reserve before it joins the column's tail at the kurgan"

msgid "Stop the wagons at the camp where Mikołaj of Michałów halts, select them and press U: they draw up into a ring. Infantry and shooters inside the ring are better armoured, and a blow in the flank costs them no spirit. In the morning the wagons go back into the column by themselves when you move them."
msgstr "Stop the wagons at the camp where Mikołaj of Michałów halts, select them and press U: they draw up into a ring. Infantry and shooters inside the ring are better armoured, and a blow in the flank costs them no spirit. In the morning the wagons go back into the column by themselves when you move them."

msgid "Stop what they are doing and stand."
msgstr "Stop what they are doing and stand."

msgid "Strike the Order's horse"
msgstr "Strike the Order's horse"

msgid "Strike the flank of the Grand Master's reserve"
msgstr "Strike the flank of the Grand Master's reserve"

msgid "Strike the iron, not the head!"
msgstr "Strike the iron, not the head!"

msgid "Sunset in %s"
msgstr "Sunset in %s"

msgid "Suspicion: %d%%"
msgstr "Suspicion: %d%%"

msgid "Tabor"
msgstr "Tabor"

msgid "Take 30 000 florins"
msgstr "Take 30 000 florins"

msgid "Take 60 000 florins"
msgstr "Take 60 000 florins"

msgid "Take Tczew"
msgstr "Take Tczew"

msgid "Take a guest knight captive"
msgstr "Take a guest knight captive"

msgid "Take all 3 places of power"
msgstr "Take all 3 places of power"

msgid "Take all 7 places of power"
msgstr "Take all 7 places of power"

msgid "Take all the bombards away to Sztum"
msgstr "Take all the bombards away to Sztum"

msgid "Take apart"
msgstr "Take apart"

msgid "Take apart: click your building"
msgstr "Take apart: click your building"

msgid "Take at least 4 bombards away to Sztum"
msgstr "Take at least 4 bombards away to Sztum"

msgid "Take at least 5 of the Order's men prisoner"
msgstr "Take at least 5 of the Order's men prisoner"

msgid "Take at least 5 princely banners captive"
msgstr "Take at least 5 princely banners captive"

msgid "Take back the sacred grove and lay an alka there"
msgstr "Take back the sacred grove and lay an alka there"

msgid "Take him to the hetman. Alive, and with honour."
msgstr "Take him to the hetman. Alive, and with honour."

msgid "Take it"
msgstr "Take it"

msgid "Take me to your prince. Let him count us along with the princes."
msgstr "Take me to your prince. Let him count us along with the princes."

msgid "Take the Muscovite camp"
msgstr "Take the Muscovite camp"

msgid "Take the Order's bombards"
msgstr "Take the Order's bombards"

msgid "Take the Order's wagon fort"
msgstr "Take the Order's wagon fort"

msgid "Take the Swedish king's loan of 2 000 florins?"
msgstr "Take the Swedish king's loan of 2 000 florins?"

msgid "Take the boyar Chelyadnin captive"
msgstr "Take the boyar Chelyadnin captive"

msgid "Take the kurgan on the west shore"
msgstr "Take the kurgan on the west shore"

msgid "Take the town wall and reach the church by the castle"
msgstr "Take the town wall and reach the church by the castle"

msgid "Take the wagenburg"
msgstr "Take the wagenburg"

msgid "Take the wagenburg together with the Lithuanians"
msgstr "Take the wagenburg together with the Lithuanians"

msgid "Takes %d population"
msgstr "Takes %d population"

msgid "Takes in: %s"
msgstr "Takes in: %s"

msgid "Talking to them is no use. Take your brothers and as many books as you can carry, and follow me. Quickly."
msgstr "Talking to them is no use. Take your brothers and as many books as you can carry, and follow me. Quickly."

msgid "Tatar captain"
msgstr "Tatar captain"

msgid "Tatars at the wagons! They came round on dry land, along the lake!"
msgstr "Tatars at the wagons! They came round on dry land, along the lake!"

msgid "Tell the Lithuanians: we fall back behind the foot not from fear. Let them not mistake it."
msgstr "Tell the Lithuanians: we fall back behind the foot not from fear. Let them not mistake it."

msgid "Tell them that the Crown will pay for this war once, not every year. And that my husband pays the same tax as they do."
msgstr "Tell them that the Crown will pay for this war once, not every year. And that my husband pays the same tax as they do."

msgid "Tell your prince: we and he have the same sovereign. And let him not tell us about faith."
msgstr "Tell your prince: we and he have the same sovereign. And let him not tell us about faith."

msgid "Ten days after Grunwald the royal army comes to the capital of the Order. Heinrich von Plauen came in before it, took command and burned the town round the castle, so that the besiegers have nowhere to shelter. Jaśko of Łęczyca has the guns of his part of the camp and the trophy bombards from Grunwald. The castle cannot be taken by storm: it can only be starved."
msgstr "Ten days after Grunwald the royal army comes to the capital of the Order. Heinrich von Plauen came in before it, took command and burned the town round the castle, so that the besiegers have nowhere to shelter. Jaśko of Łęczyca has the guns of his part of the camp and the trophy bombards from Grunwald. The castle cannot be taken by storm: it can only be starved."

msgid "Ten days we marched here. And in ten days he managed to burn everything that could burn."
msgstr "Ten days we marched here. And in ten days he managed to burn everything that could burn."

msgid "Text size"
msgstr "Text size"

msgid "Thank him and refuse"
msgstr "Thank him and refuse"

msgid "That day they took the hetman captive, Prince Konstanty, wounded. And with him Marshal Hryhory Ostikovich, Marshal Litavor Khreptovich, the princes Drutsky and Mosalsky and many others. The wagons and the guns stayed beyond the river."
msgstr "That day they took the hetman captive, Prince Konstanty, wounded. And with him Marshal Hryhory Ostikovich, Marshal Litavor Khreptovich, the princes Drutsky and Mosalsky and many others. The wagons and the guns stayed beyond the river."

msgid "That is exactly what they do not like. Get up and run to the royal banner, before they get here."
msgstr "That is exactly what they do not like. Get up and run to the royal banner, before they get here."

msgid "That is their forward regiment. Tell the prince."
msgstr "That is their forward regiment. Tell the prince."

msgid "That is why we stand here. When everybody runs one way, somebody has to look the other."
msgstr "That is why we stand here. When everybody runs one way, somebody has to look the other."

msgid "That scribe was Zbigniew Oleśnicki, later a cardinal. And the German Długosz calls Dypold Kökeritz of Lusatia. I am a scribe myself and love this story more than any other."
msgstr "That scribe was Zbigniew Oleśnicki, later a cardinal. And the German Długosz calls Dypold Kökeritz of Lusatia. I am a scribe myself and love this story more than any other."

msgid "That year Prince Michael Glinski, a learned and proud man, killed his enemy, Lord Zabrzeziński, and raised a revolt. He called the Ruthenian princes to follow him, and he called for help from Moscow. The princess of Slutsk did not follow him."
msgstr "That year Prince Michael Glinski, a learned and proud man, killed his enemy, Lord Zabrzeziński, and raised a revolt. He called the Ruthenian princes to follow him, and he called for help from Moscow. The princess of Slutsk did not follow him."

msgid "That year Samogitia was German. Vytautas gave it to the Order by treaty, and nobody asked us. Last winter there was hunger. King Jogaila sent us grain down the river, but the Germans stopped the boats and said they would feed Samogitia themselves."
msgstr "That year Samogitia was German. Vytautas gave it to the Order by treaty, and nobody asked us. Last winter there was hunger. King Jogaila sent us grain down the river, but the Germans stopped the boats and said they would feed Samogitia themselves."

msgid "The Banner and the Silver"
msgstr "The Banner and the Silver"

msgid "The Dnieper above Orsha and the field between the Dnieper and the Kropivna. The night of 7 to 8 September 1514."
msgstr "The Dnieper above Orsha and the field between the Dnieper and the Kropivna. The night of 7 to 8 September 1514."

msgid "The Gdańsk council will lend the Crown money. How much will you take? Every loan angers the town, and every next one more."
msgstr "The Gdańsk council will lend the Crown money. How much will you take? Every loan angers the town, and every next one more."

msgid "The Gdańsk gate of Chojnice swings open. A small troop comes out, two hundred men, and does not go to the field but turns to the king's tent. Trumpets, shouting."
msgstr "The Gdańsk gate of Chojnice swings open. A small troop comes out, two hundred men, and does not go to the field but turns to the king's tent. Trumpets, shouting."

msgid "The Germans will go. The grove will go too. Not at once. The fire will go under the ground and stay there while somebody remembers it."
msgstr "The Germans will go. The grove will go too. Not at once. The fire will go under the ground and stay there while somebody remembers it."

msgid "The Gintovts', prince. From the Dnieper."
msgstr "The Gintovts', prince. From the Dnieper."

msgid "The Grand Master at the window turns and looks at Stach. He says nothing."
msgstr "The Grand Master at the window turns and looks at Stach. He says nothing."

msgid "The Grand Master had been taken out of the castle earlier, to Chojnice, and from there he got away to Königsberg. The brothers left with their archive and their relics, and nobody touched them. For almost a century and a half Malbork had been the capital of the Order, and the Order left it on foot."
msgstr "The Grand Master had been taken out of the castle earlier, to Chojnice, and from there he got away to Königsberg. The brothers left with their archive and their relics, and nobody touched them. For almost a century and a half Malbork had been the capital of the Order, and the Order left it on foot."

msgid "The Grand Master leads his reserve round our wing, at the king's hill. Two fresh banners from the king's reserve have come up by Stębark. Keep men by the king, do not throw everything into the fight."
msgstr "The Grand Master leads his reserve round our wing, at the king's hill. Two fresh banners from the king's reserve have come up by Stębark. Keep men by the king, do not throw everything into the fight."

msgid "The Grand Master's reserve breaks the Polish centre while you are away"
msgstr "The Grand Master's reserve breaks the Polish centre while you are away"

msgid "The Grand Master's reserve broke the Polish centre while the Lithuanians were away."
msgstr "The Grand Master's reserve broke the Polish centre while the Lithuanians were away."

msgid "The Left Hand rides at your horse. Set the rally point by the guns (Shift + right click), then order the «Lithuanian retreat»: today the riders go all the way to the rally point, and the chase follows them."
msgstr "The Left Hand rides at your horse. Set the rally point by the guns (Shift + right click), then order the «Lithuanian retreat»: today the riders go all the way to the rally point, and the chase follows them."

msgid "The Lithuanians have run! They have left us here alone!"
msgstr "The Lithuanians have run! They have left us here alone!"

msgid "The Livonian Master fell, and his marshal, and many commanders. And Švitrigaila got away to Polotsk with thirty men, as three years before. That road must have been well known to him."
msgstr "The Livonian Master fell, and his marshal, and many commanders. And Švitrigaila got away to Polotsk with thirty men, as three years before. That road must have been well known to him."

msgid "The Livonian vanguard gets away with most of its men"
msgstr "The Livonian vanguard gets away with most of its men"

msgid "The Livonian vanguard got away to Vilkomir with most of its men. Švitrigaila will come back."
msgstr "The Livonian vanguard got away to Vilkomir with most of its men. Švitrigaila will come back."

msgid "The Livonians turn back and push along the dry strip. Their marshal Nesselrode and Master Kerskorf ride with them."
msgstr "The Livonians turn back and push along the dry strip. Their marshal Nesselrode and Master Kerskorf ride with them."

msgid "The Lower cannot be held! Everyone to the Upper, townsmen first, spears close the way!"
msgstr "The Lower cannot be held! Everyone to the Upper, townsmen first, spears close the way!"

msgid "The Lower castle is lost"
msgstr "The Lower castle is lost"

msgid "The Masovians too. And pan Andrzej of Tęczyn, they say, misses his wife."
msgstr "The Masovians too. And pan Andrzej of Tęczyn, they say, misses his wife."

msgid "The Master is down! Killed in the press!"
msgstr "The Master is down! Killed in the press!"

msgid "The Master is gone! Killed in the melee!"
msgstr "The Master is gone! Killed in the melee!"

msgid "The Master was found among the dead, with wounds in the forehead and the chest. The next day the king had the body sent to Malbork. And all his life Jaśko looked for the man in red, to ask how much he owed. He found him forty-four years later."
msgstr "The Master was found among the dead, with wounds in the forehead and the chest. The next day the king had the body sent to Malbork. And all his life Jaśko looked for the man in red, to ask how much he owed. He found him forty-four years later."

msgid "The Muscovite horse flies into the ravine at full gallop. Out of the bushes the foot rises. A volley. The smoke covers half the field."
msgstr "The Muscovite horse flies into the ravine at full gallop. Out of the bushes the foot rises. A volley. The smoke covers half the field."

msgid "The Oak and the Chase"
msgstr "The Oak and the Chase"

msgid "The Order has gathered enough evidence. The council believed that the Samogitians were baptized in name only."
msgstr "The Order has gathered enough evidence. The council believed that the Samogitians were baptized in name only."

msgid "The Order is beaten at Grunwald."
msgstr "The Order is beaten at Grunwald."

msgid "The Order is gathering evidence for the council. Every rite a spy sees brings defeat closer. A spy is struck only on your order, and a killed spy is evidence too."
msgstr "The Order is gathering evidence for the council. Every rite a spy sees brings defeat closer. A spy is struck only on your order, and a killed spy is evidence too."

msgid "The Order lost about a thousand dead that day and some fifty prisoners, the Poles about a hundred dead and as many again who died of their wounds. Raweneck was buried at Żarnowiec. It was the first battle in the open field the royal army won in that war, and the war turned."
msgstr "The Order lost about a thousand dead that day and some fifty prisoners, the Poles about a hundred dead and as many again who died of their wounds. Raweneck was buried at Żarnowiec. It was the first battle in the open field the royal army won in that war, and the war turned."

msgid "The Order's army comes out from behind the hill and sets its own wagons on the rise across the field: horse in front of the wagons, foot behind them."
msgstr "The Order's army comes out from behind the hill and sets its own wagons on the rise across the field: horse in front of the wagons, foot behind them."

msgid "The Order's evidence reaches 100"
msgstr "The Order's evidence reaches 100"

msgid "The Order's horse moves off all together. The earth hums."
msgstr "The Order's horse moves off all together. The earth hums."

msgid "The Order's horse rode in under the crossbows and lay down there. But many of ours fell in that hour too; among them the Gdańsk councillor Maciej Hagen, whose name is written down. And Dunin took a second wound and went back into the saddle again."
msgstr "The Order's horse rode in under the crossbows and lay down there. But many of ours fell in that hour too; among them the Gdańsk councillor Maciej Hagen, whose name is written down. And Dunin took a second wound and went back into the saddle again."

msgid "The Order's horse runs to the town walls, and the levy rides after it by itself. Keep your banners here: tell them to stand (C)."
msgstr "The Order's horse runs to the town walls, and the levy rides after it by itself. Keep your banners here: tell them to stand (C)."

msgid "The Order's knechts hold out behind the chained wagons. Break in and cut them down."
msgstr "The Order's knechts hold out behind the chained wagons. Break in and cut them down."

msgid "The Order's men are in the Polish wagon fort. The battle is lost."
msgstr "The Order's men are in the Polish wagon fort. The battle is lost."

msgid "The Order's men who run or have lost heart lay down their arms when your men come up to them: they are prisoners, and every one is ransomed for silver. The foot in the wagon fort yields one by one while your men stand inside it."
msgstr "The Order's men who run or have lost heart lay down their arms when your men come up to them: they are prisoners, and every one is ransomed for silver. The foot in the wagon fort yields one by one while your men stand inside it."

msgid "The Order's riders have come over the Nogat. They plunder villages and go for loaded wagons. A plundered village pays nothing until the next season; every rider killed brings 1 000 florins of booty."
msgstr "The Order's riders have come over the Nogat. They plunder villages and go for loaded wagons. A plundered village pays nothing until the next season; every rider killed brings 1 000 florins of booty."

msgid "The Order's tithe collector is coming up the road."
msgstr "The Order's tithe collector is coming up the road."

msgid "The Order's wagons are taken, with their guns and all their goods. And on the west road, from the forest, people are coming: the Pomeranian peasants who had been called to the Order's army and came late."
msgstr "The Order's wagons are taken, with their guns and all their goods. And on the west road, from the forest, people are coming: the Pomeranian peasants who had been called to the Order's army and came late."

msgid "The Poles are still singing. So it is time. To horse!"
msgstr "The Poles are still singing. So it is time. To horse!"

msgid "The Polish wagon fort is taken"
msgstr "The Polish wagon fort is taken"

msgid "The Prussian Bitschin writes that Čapek rode into the sea and made a speech beginning with the words: «Behold, brothers, I bear witness to you…» But Bitschin called Čapek a robber and could put anything in his mouth. That they filled bottles with the water and carried them home, everyone writes."
msgstr "The Prussian Bitschin writes that Čapek rode into the sea and made a speech beginning with the words: «Behold, brothers, I bear witness to you…» But Bitschin called Čapek a robber and could put anything in his mouth. That they filled bottles with the water and carried them home, everyone writes."

msgid "The Thirteen Years' War is in its ninth year. Both sides fight with hired men and neither has the money to pay them; the king pays with the silver of the Prussian towns, Gdańsk first of all. Piotr Dunin has brought the royal mercenaries and the Gdańsk men to Świecino, and the Order's hired army under Fritz Raweneck is coming against them. Stach of Łęczyca, twenty-seven, a captain of a royal company now, counts the silver for his men."
msgstr "The Thirteen Years' War is in its ninth year. Both sides fight with hired men and neither has the money to pay them; the king pays with the silver of the Prussian towns, Gdańsk first of all. Piotr Dunin has brought the royal mercenaries and the Gdańsk men to Świecino, and the Order's hired army under Fritz Raweneck is coming against them. Stach of Łęczyca, twenty-seven, a captain of a royal company now, counts the silver for his men."

msgid "The Upper castle is taken"
msgstr "The Upper castle is taken"

msgid "The abbey among its orchards. Czech infantry with torches goes to the gate. A young monk runs out and falls on his knees before the Crown's horsemen."
msgstr "The abbey among its orchards. Czech infantry with torches goes to the gate. A young monk runs out and falls on his knees before the Crown's horsemen."

msgid "The alarm is up! The watch rides to where it saw you, and the chase will come sooner. Get away into the forest."
msgstr "The alarm is up! The watch rides to where it saw you, and the chase will come sooner. Get away into the forest."

msgid "The alka gives Power. Every place of power you hold with an alka adds more; near the Order's castles and priests it gives less."
msgstr "The alka gives Power. Every place of power you hold with an alka adds more; near the Order's castles and priests it gives less."

msgid "The armies of King Jogaila and Grand Duke Vytautas stand against the Order of Grand Master Ulrich von Jungingen. Gintaut and his Samogitians are in the right wing, under the hand of Vytautas. The Lithuanian wing will be the first to hear the trumpet."
msgstr "The armies of King Jogaila and Grand Duke Vytautas stand against the Order of Grand Master Ulrich von Jungingen. Gintaut and his Samogitians are in the right wing, under the hand of Vytautas. The Lithuanian wing will be the first to hear the trumpet."

msgid "The armies of King Władysław Jagiełło and Grand Duke Vytautas stand against the Order of Grand Master Ulrich von Jungingen. The Poles hold the left wing, the Lithuanians the right. Jaśko of Łęczyca, twenty-two years old, in borrowed armour on a borrowed horse, waits with the lances of the left wing in the shade of a grove, while the Order stands in the sun."
msgstr "The armies of King Władysław Jagiełło and Grand Duke Vytautas stand against the Order of Grand Master Ulrich von Jungingen. The Poles hold the left wing, the Lithuanians the right. Jaśko of Łęczyca, twenty-two years old, in borrowed armour on a borrowed horse, waits with the lances of the left wing in the shade of a grove, while the Order stands in the sun."

msgid "The army crosses the bridge onto Mitkovo field. Your place is the right edge of the line, towards the Dnieper. There is no more hiring: the battle has begun."
msgstr "The army crosses the bridge onto Mitkovo field. Your place is the right edge of the line, towards the Dnieper. There is no more hiring: the battle has begun."

msgid "The army goes south across the reaped fields. The Czech wagons creak; on one of them someone's trophy church vestments, tied on in place of a cover, are burning."
msgstr "The army goes south across the reaped fields. The Czech wagons creak; on one of them someone's trophy church vestments, tied on in place of a cover, are burning."

msgid "The army has come to the sea. The Order agrees to a truce."
msgstr "The army has come to the sea. The Order agrees to a truce."

msgid "The banner has fallen! Bring a rider to it within 20 seconds."
msgstr "The banner has fallen! Bring a rider to it within 20 seconds."

msgid "The banner is up again."
msgstr "The banner is up again."

msgid "The banner lies on the ground: %s"
msgstr "The banner lies on the ground: %s"

msgid "The banner rises. All along the line the Poles roar. Jaśko looks round: there is nobody in red beside him."
msgstr "The banner rises. All along the line the Poles roar. Jaśko looks round: there is nobody in red beside him."

msgid "The banner! After me, whoever is in the saddle!"
msgstr "The banner! After me, whoever is in the saddle!"

msgid "The battle on the Vedrosha is lost, but Andrei has brought his men back over the Trosna."
msgstr "The battle on the Vedrosha is lost, but Andrei has brought his men back over the Trosna."

msgid "The beginning of September. On the eastern edge a column under Livonian banners halts. Vytautas rides out to meet it with his banners. From afar one can see the riders come together, talk and part."
msgstr "The beginning of September. On the eastern edge a column under Livonian banners halts. Vytautas rides out to meet it with his banners. From afar one can see the riders come together, talk and part."

msgid "The bloody flux has emptied the camp. There is nobody left to hold the guns."
msgstr "The bloody flux has emptied the camp. There is nobody left to hold the guns."

msgid "The boyar! We have taken the boyar himself!"
msgstr "The boyar! We have taken the boyar himself!"

msgid "The broken banners of the Order hold out behind the chained wagons by Grunwald. Break in and cut them down."
msgstr "The broken banners of the Order hold out behind the chained wagons by Grunwald. Break in and cut them down."

msgid "The burned church gave the Order 25 evidence. Build a new one: chapter 4 needs churches."
msgstr "The burned church gave the Order 25 evidence. Build a new one: chapter 4 needs churches."

msgid "The camp is up in arms! Bring the sortie back into the castle before the riders close in."
msgstr "The camp is up in arms! Bring the sortie back into the castle before the riders close in."

msgid "The camp servants build a battery of wicker gabions. A bombard fires only from a battery: bring it to one and let it stand still. Every shot costs 5 powder, and powder comes slower than it goes."
msgstr "The camp servants build a battery of wicker gabions. A bombard fires only from a battery: bring it to one and let it stand still. Every shot costs 5 powder, and powder comes slower than it goes."

msgid "The capital and castles of the losing side are destroyed."
msgstr "The capital and castles of the losing side are destroyed."

msgid "The captains of free companies have come to the camp. Whom will you hire on the Gdańsk silver? Every hired man wants his pay on each payday too: in the morning and at noon."
msgstr "The captains of free companies have come to the camp. Whom will you hire on the Gdańsk silver? Every hired man wants his pay on each payday too: in the morning and at noon."

msgid "The cart goes by itself along the trail to the north. It cannot fight: guard it."
msgstr "The cart goes by itself along the trail to the north. It cannot fight: guard it."

msgid "The castellan of Łęczyca, Wojciech Bniński, wounded in the head, gave himself up to Plauen himself. That is written. And the banner of his land, pan Jan said, old Jaśko caught up."
msgstr "The castellan of Łęczyca, Wojciech Bniński, wounded in the head, gave himself up to Plauen himself. That is written. And the banner of his land, pan Jan said, old Jaśko caught up."

msgid "The castle at Skirsnemune burned, and the knights who sat in it were killed. Both our books and the German ones write of it. But there was still Dubysa, where the vogt himself sat."
msgstr "The castle at Skirsnemune burned, and the knights who sat in it were killed. Both our books and the German ones write of it. But there was still Dubysa, where the vogt himself sat."

msgid "The castle gate. Some dozens of brothers in white cloaks come out on foot, and behind them wagons with the chests of the archive and with relics under covers. Polish soldiers stand on both sides of the road. Somebody reaches for a crossbow."
msgstr "The castle gate. Some dozens of brothers in white cloaks come out on foot, and behind them wagons with the chests of the archive and with relics under covers. Polish soldiers stand on both sides of the road. Somebody reaches for a crossbow."

msgid "The castle's guns answer the nearest battery. The burned walls round the town fall when a ball strikes them: do not keep men under them."
msgstr "The castle's guns answer the nearest battery. The burned walls round the town fall when a ball strikes them: do not keep men under them."

msgid "The chase did not come to the guns. The hetman orders the general attack all the same."
msgstr "The chase did not come to the guns. The hetman orders the general attack all the same."

msgid "The chase holds the ford before the prince is across"
msgstr "The chase holds the ford before the prince is across"

msgid "The chase is at the ford! Cross to meet it or strike from the bank."
msgstr "The chase is at the ford! Cross to meet it or strike from the bank."

msgid "The chase sets out in %s"
msgstr "The chase sets out in %s"

msgid "The chase took the ford before the prince was across."
msgstr "The chase took the ford before the prince was across."

msgid "The church stands on the hill over the stream. The place of power there has gone out for good, but faith grows twice as fast."
msgstr "The church stands on the hill over the stream. The place of power there has gone out for good, but faith grows twice as fast."

msgid "The column's head is making for the Šventoji ford and Vilkomir! If most of the Livonians get away, the battle is lost."
msgstr "The column's head is making for the Šventoji ford and Vilkomir! If most of the Livonians get away, the battle is lost."

msgid "The concord has broken down twice. The orphans turn their wagons home to Bohemia."
msgstr "The concord has broken down twice. The orphans turn their wagons home to Bohemia."

msgid "The concord has fallen to nothing: for a while the orphans stand where they are and follow nobody. If it happens again, they go home."
msgstr "The concord has fallen to nothing: for a while the orphans stand where they are and follow nobody. If it happens again, they go home."

msgid "The concord with the orphans breaks down twice"
msgstr "The concord with the orphans breaks down twice"

msgid "The council has decided. We will not buy the gate."
msgstr "The council has decided. We will not buy the gate."

msgid "The council's envoys have been killed on Samogitian land."
msgstr "The council's envoys have been killed on Samogitian land."

msgid "The cross becomes a chapel: Power %s a second instead of %s."
msgstr "The cross becomes a chapel: Power %s a second instead of %s."

msgid "The crossbowmen"
msgstr "The crossbowmen"

msgid "The crowd of peasants with scythes and flails stops. The first ones look at the wagons on the rise."
msgstr "The crowd of peasants with scythes and flails stops. The first ones look at the wagons on the rise."

msgid "The delegation's cart has been destroyed. Nobody will speak for Samogitia at Konstanz."
msgstr "The delegation's cart has been destroyed. Nobody will speak for Samogitia at Konstanz."

msgid "The delegation's cart or the council's envoys are destroyed"
msgstr "The delegation's cart or the council's envoys are destroyed"

msgid "The envoys stop in each of the three villages on the way and go on once a church stands there. Lay the next church before they come."
msgstr "The envoys stop in each of the three villages on the way and go on once a church stands there. Lay the next church before they come."

msgid "The evening of the seventh of September. The camp by the Dnieper. At the entrance to the hetman's tent sits a scribe with an inkwell at his belt. Andrei comes up. The scribe reads his name in the list and looks up."
msgstr "The evening of the seventh of September. The camp by the Dnieper. At the entrance to the hetman's tent sits a scribe with an inkwell at his belt. Andrei comes up. The scribe reads his name in the list and looks up."

msgid "The evidence at the top right is what the Order can show the council. At 100 the mission is lost. Every baptized peasant slows it down."
msgstr "The evidence at the top right is what the Order can show the council. At 100 the mission is lost. Every baptized peasant slows it down."

msgid "The field before Chojnice, Gdańsk Pomerania. 18 September 1454, from morning to night."
msgstr "The field before Chojnice, Gdańsk Pomerania. 18 September 1454, from morning to night."

msgid "The field between Grunwald, Stębark and Ludwikowo, Prussia. 15 July 1410."
msgstr "The field between Grunwald, Stębark and Ludwikowo, Prussia. 15 July 1410."

msgid "The field by Grunwald, Prussia. 15 July 1410."
msgstr "The field by Grunwald, Prussia. 15 July 1410."

msgid "The fight on the causeway. When the eye comes back to it, there is nobody on the causeway: neither Jaśko, nor the man in red."
msgstr "The fight on the causeway. When the eye comes back to it, there is nobody on the causeway: neither Jaśko, nor the man in red."

msgid "The fire in the alka has gone under the ground: the grove gives half its Power from now on."
msgstr "The fire in the alka has gone under the ground: the grove gives half its Power from now on."

msgid "The first bridge stands. The foot and the guns can go over it slowly, a few at a time."
msgstr "The first bridge stands. The foot and the guns can go over it slowly, a few at a time."

msgid "The first on the wall was Jakub of Kobylany, and after him Dobiesław of Oleśnica. Twenty-five years later Jakub will lead the Crown's knights at Wiłkomierz, but that is another story, and I have told it already."
msgstr "The first on the wall was Jakub of Kobylany, and after him Dobiesław of Oleśnica. Twenty-five years later Jakub will lead the Crown's knights at Wiłkomierz, but that is another story, and I have told it already."

msgid "The flood has covered the low meadows: wagons go along the dikes. The boats are free again."
msgstr "The flood has covered the low meadows: wagons go along the dikes. The boats are free again."

msgid "The foot servants"
msgstr "The foot servants"

msgid "The ford is upstream, to the east: the light horse and the lances can cross it, the guns cannot. Send the camp servants to the two marked places on the bank: standing there they lay a bridge section by section (40 wood each, the wagons bring more). A Muscovite patrol rides the far bank at night: if it watches your men for long, the alarm goes up."
msgstr "The ford is upstream, to the east: the light horse and the lances can cross it, the guns cannot. Send the camp servants to the two marked places on the bank: standing there they lay a bridge section by section (40 wood each, the wagons bring more). A Muscovite patrol rides the far bank at night: if it watches your men for long, the alarm goes up."

msgid "The ford lies below the bridge, towards the Dnieper. No more than two in it at once: whoever crowds in drowns. Leave a rearguard on the near bank. Four light horse whose standard-bearer fell have joined you."
msgstr "The ford lies below the bridge, towards the Dnieper. No more than two in it at once: whoever crowds in drowns. Leave a rearguard on the near bank. Four light horse whose standard-bearer fell have joined you."

msgid "The forest borderland of Muscovy and the Grand Duchy of Lithuania. The end of August or September 1507."
msgstr "The forest borderland of Muscovy and the Grand Duchy of Lithuania. The end of August or September 1507."

msgid "The games differ in rules or data; both players need the same build"
msgstr "The games differ in rules or data; both players need the same build"

msgid "The garrison has broken into the royal camp and ruined the king's tent."
msgstr "The garrison has broken into the royal camp and ruined the king's tent."

msgid "The garrison sends riders to catch the envoys. An envoy with an enemy at his side and none of ours near is taken. Every sworn town sends food, powder or silver."
msgstr "The garrison sends riders to catch the envoys. An envoy with an enemy at his side and none of ours near is taken. Every sworn town sends food, powder or silver."

msgid "The gate burns through and falls. The Poles go in over the burning suburb."
msgstr "The gate burns through and falls. The Poles go in over the burning suburb."

msgid "The gate! The commander sends his horse after the wagons!"
msgstr "The gate! The commander sends his horse after the wagons!"

msgid "The general attack! The foot and the guns are yours again, and the hetman gives you ten more banners of horse. Chelyadnin will throw his reserves into the field one after another. Muscovite banners that have lost heart and are caught between your men from two sides give themselves up."
msgstr "The general attack! The foot and the guns are yours again, and the hetman gives you ten more banners of horse. Chelyadnin will throw his reserves into the field one after another. Muscovite banners that have lost heart and are caught between your men from two sides give themselves up."

msgid "The grandson owes me nothing."
msgstr "The grandson owes me nothing."

msgid "The great banner of the kingdom lies in the dust. The Polish banners waver and break."
msgstr "The great banner of the kingdom lies in the dust. The Polish banners waver and break."

msgid "The great banner of the kingdom lies on the ground longer than 60 seconds"
msgstr "The great banner of the kingdom lies on the ground longer than 60 seconds"

msgid "The grove is there still. My grandfather Mikołaj used to say he had a brother, Jurij, who went away east."
msgstr "The grove is there still. My grandfather Mikołaj used to say he had a brother, Jurij, who went away east."

msgid "The heart of your land: trains peasants, takes in every resource and leads your people into the next age. In a skirmish, a side that loses every town centre and castle is out."
msgstr "The heart of your land: trains peasants, takes in every resource and leads your people into the next age. In a skirmish, a side that loses every town centre and castle is out."

msgid "The hetman and his army are on the road to Orsha. Glinski has no time for Slutsk now."
msgstr "The hetman and his army are on the road to Orsha. Glinski has no time for Slutsk now."

msgid "The hetman himself said afterwards that a local woman who knew the paths led him through the bog. But Andrei swore that he saw wolves that night, going along the bank in a pack, and all of them one way."
msgstr "The hetman himself said afterwards that a local woman who knew the paths led him through the bog. But Andrei swore that he saw wolves that night, going along the bank in a pack, and all of them one way."

msgid "The hetman leaves last, standard-bearer. Lead your men away. That is an order."
msgstr "The hetman leaves last, standard-bearer. Lead your men away. That is an order."

msgid "The hetman's headquarters falls or the army is thrown into the Dnieper"
msgstr "The hetman's headquarters falls or the army is thrown into the Dnieper"

msgid "The hetman's headquarters has fallen. The army breaks and runs for the river."
msgstr "The hetman's headquarters has fallen. The army breaks and runs for the river."

msgid "The hetman's ring holds: %s"
msgstr "The hetman's ring holds: %s"

msgid "The hints at the top left can be turned off in the settings."
msgstr "The hints at the top left can be turned off in the settings."

msgid "The horse is good. The grandson is better. His to go, mine to stand. Do not touch the grandson."
msgstr "The horse is good. The grandson is better. His to go, mine to stand. Do not touch the grandson."

msgid "The horses are in a lather. Change the companies, take the tired ones back to the wagons!"
msgstr "The horses are in a lather. Change the companies, take the tired ones back to the wagons!"

msgid "The horses are ready, prince."
msgstr "The horses are ready, prince."

msgid "The horses in the forest are moving! The ambush will strike in half a minute."
msgstr "The horses in the forest are moving! The ambush will strike in half a minute."

msgid "The khan is taking his men away. Don't stand there, Lithuanian, or you will stay here for good."
msgstr "The khan is taking his men away. Don't stand there, Lithuanian, or you will stay here for good."

msgid "The king fights and will not leave by himself. Surround him with 3 of your units: he gives himself up to his own men and rides with them to the causeway while they stay beside him."
msgstr "The king fights and will not leave by himself. Surround him with 3 of your units: he gives himself up to his own men and rides with them to the causeway while they stay beside him."

msgid "The king has been taken by the Order's hirelings. Nobody will ransom the Crown."
msgstr "The king has been taken by the Order's hirelings. Nobody will ransom the Crown."

msgid "The king has fallen. The army has lost its head."
msgstr "The king has fallen. The army has lost its head."

msgid "The king is killed or taken"
msgstr "The king is killed or taken"

msgid "The king is over the bog."
msgstr "The king is over the bog."

msgid "The king orders."
msgstr "The king orders."

msgid "The king orders: do not go into the breach! Fall back to the church!"
msgstr "The king orders: do not go into the breach! Fall back to the church!"

msgid "The king rides past with his suite. He looks at the castle for a long time and says nothing."
msgstr "The king rides past with his suite. He looks at the castle for a long time and says nothing."

msgid "The king wrote afterwards to the sovereigns and to Rome that the Muscovites were eighty thousand and that thirty thousand of them fell or were taken. I wrote the lists of captives in my own hand, and I know that kings count otherwise than scribes do. The master of the horse Chelyadnin we took captive, and Smolensk we never won back."
msgstr "The king wrote afterwards to the sovereigns and to Rome that the Muscovites were eighty thousand and that thirty thousand of them fell or were taken. I wrote the lists of captives in my own hand, and I know that kings count otherwise than scribes do. The master of the horse Chelyadnin we took captive, and Smolensk we never won back."

msgid "The king's hill. A lone knight of the Order with his lance lowered rides straight at Jagiełło. A young scribe without armour catches up a broken lance and strikes the knight in the side; he falls. The king strikes him with his own lance, the guard finishes him."
msgstr "The king's hill. A lone knight of the Order with his lance lowered rides straight at Jagiełło. A young scribe without armour catches up a broken lance and strikes the knight in the side; he falls. The king strikes him with his own lance, the guard finishes him."

msgid "The king's signal. Strike the Order's horse with the whole banner."
msgstr "The king's signal. Strike the Order's horse with the whole banner."

msgid "The king's tent is ruined"
msgstr "The king's tent is ruined"

msgid "The king's word. The Crown is ready to pay for the castle."
msgstr "The king's word. The Crown is ready to pay for the castle."

msgid "The knights are coming out! Don't let them reach the boats!"
msgstr "The knights are coming out! Don't let them reach the boats!"

msgid "The knights dubbed on the shore at Oliwa in 1433 have come with Jaśko. Grey now, like him."
msgstr "The knights dubbed on the shore at Oliwa in 1433 have come with Jaśko. Grey now, like him."

msgid "The lance beside Gintaut carries his banner. Units near it keep their spirit. If the bearer falls, bring a rider to the banner within 20 seconds, or the khorugv runs."
msgstr "The lance beside Gintaut carries his banner. Units near it keep their spirit. If the bearer falls, bring a rider to the banner within 20 seconds, or the khorugv runs."

msgid "The lances"
msgstr "The lances"

msgid "The last capital cannot be taken apart"
msgstr "The last capital cannot be taken apart"

msgid "The last village, my lord. From here the road goes to Medininkai."
msgstr "The last village, my lord. From here the road goes to Medininkai."

msgid "The levy of the nobility: brave, but wilful. Seeing an enemy run, they ride after him by themselves unless they are told to stand (C). Their spirit falls quickly, and comes back quicker by their banner."
msgstr "The levy of the nobility: brave, but wilful. Seeing an enemy run, they ride after him by themselves unless they are told to stand (C). Their spirit falls quickly, and comes back quicker by their banner."

msgid "The lone oak on the hill is a place of power. Take it, and the znakharka can lay an alka there for Power."
msgstr "The lone oak on the hill is a place of power. Take it, and the znakharka can lay an alka there for Power."

msgid "The lord vogt demands grain for the castles. You wanted to be protected, did you not?"
msgstr "The lord vogt demands grain for the castles. You wanted to be protected, did you not?"

msgid "The losing side gave up."
msgstr "The losing side gave up."

msgid "The marshal's banner is down! Press on, lords, before they raise another!"
msgstr "The marshal's banner is down! Press on, lords, before they raise another!"

msgid "The mercenaries' patience is at an end. Červenka has sold Malbork back to the Order."
msgstr "The mercenaries' patience is at an end. Červenka has sold Malbork back to the Order."

msgid "The mercenaries' patience runs out"
msgstr "The mercenaries' patience runs out"

msgid "The mist lies over the grove. The envoys pass by without seeing the oak."
msgstr "The mist lies over the grove. The envoys pass by without seeing the oak."

msgid "The money for Malbork was to be found by Stach's elder sister Barbara, the wife of a Gdańsk merchant, who knew the Żuławy like her own kitchen."
msgstr "The money for Malbork was to be found by Stach's elder sister Barbara, the wife of a Gdańsk merchant, who knew the Żuławy like her own kitchen."

msgid "The night before 17 September 1462. The Polish camp at Świecino. Fires, wagons, the clink of chains: the wagoners are chaining the wheels together. Stach sits on a wagon shaft and by the light of a candle counts the purses of silver for his company. On the next shaft sits a man in a red coat. The wagoners do not see him."
msgstr "The night before 17 September 1462. The Polish camp at Świecino. Fires, wagons, the clink of chains: the wagoners are chaining the wheels together. Stach sits on a wagon shaft and by the light of a candle counts the purses of silver for his company. On the next shaft sits a man in a red coat. The wagoners do not see him."

msgid "The nobility of Greater Poland stands in the first rank, it has always been so! Let the Kuyavians stand behind us."
msgstr "The nobility of Greater Poland stands in the first rank, it has always been so! Let the Kuyavians stand behind us."

msgid "The noon rest"
msgstr "The noon rest"

msgid "The north side is open now. The sorties will come out of the north gate too."
msgstr "The north side is open now. The sorties will come out of the north gate too."

msgid "The northern camp. The Lithuanians are striking their tents. The Tatars drive their herds from the meadows. Vytautas rides up to the king's tent, pale."
msgstr "The northern camp. The Lithuanians are striking their tents. The Tatars drive their herds from the meadows. Vytautas rides up to the king's tent, pale."

msgid "The oak has fallen and the alka with it: the evidence fell by 20. The pagans at the farmstead grow in number."
msgstr "The oak has fallen and the alka with it: the evidence fell by 20. The pagans at the farmstead grow in number."

msgid "The old branch of our family stayed in Samogitia and Vilnius. The younger went to the Dnieper, became Orthodox and served the princes. Andrei Gintovt was of the younger branch. That year he was twenty, and he carried the banner for the first time."
msgstr "The old branch of our family stayed in Samogitia and Vilnius. The younger went to the Dnieper, became Orthodox and served the princes. Andrei Gintovt was of the younger branch. That year he was twenty, and he carried the banner for the first time."

msgid "The old men argued afterwards who led ours then: the sword-bearer Zyndram or the marshal. Jaśko remembered Zyndram, because he shouted louder than anyone."
msgstr "The old men argued afterwards who led ours then: the sword-bearer Zyndram or the marshal. Jaśko remembered Zyndram, because he shouted louder than anyone."

msgid "The old oak above the Kropivna has given one charge of Power: the znakharka can lay «Bog Mist» once. Under the mist the guns stay hidden even outside the ravine."
msgstr "The old oak above the Kropivna has given one charge of Power: the znakharka can lay «Bog Mist» once. Under the mist the guns stay hidden even outside the ravine."

msgid "The old woman does not answer and goes ahead without looking back. The prince gets down and leads his horse by the bridle. The barking behind them falters and goes off to one side, as if the patrol had turned the wrong way. In the middle of the causeway the old woman is gone; only the lantern hangs on a pole."
msgstr "The old woman does not answer and goes ahead without looking back. The prince gets down and leads his horse by the bridle. The barking behind them falters and goes off to one side, as if the patrol had turned the wrong way. In the middle of the causeway the old woman is gone; only the lantern hangs on a pole."

msgid "The orphans listen to nobody"
msgstr "The orphans listen to nobody"

msgid "The orphans reach the prisoners: %s"
msgstr "The orphans reach the prisoners: %s"

msgid "The other bank. Dawn twilight. Andrei with a patrol by the water."
msgstr "The other bank. Dawn twilight. Andrei with a patrol by the water."

msgid "The other game sent a start this game cannot read"
msgstr "The other game sent a start this game cannot read"

msgid "The other player has left the game"
msgstr "The other player has left the game"

msgid "The pagans are coming out of the farmstead again."
msgstr "The pagans are coming out of the farmstead again."

msgid "The pagans are going for the new church."
msgstr "The pagans are going for the new church."

msgid "The pagans from the farmstead are coming for the church. You can buy peace at the farmstead: bring Gintaut there."
msgstr "The pagans from the farmstead are coming for the church. You can buy peace at the farmstead: bring Gintaut there."

msgid "The pagans lie in wait on the hills!"
msgstr "The pagans lie in wait on the hills!"

msgid "The pagans will leave you alone for the rest of this chapter."
msgstr "The pagans will leave you alone for the rest of this chapter."

msgid "The panic reached the camp. Zinnenberg's captor fell, and Zinnenberg himself was free again and led the pursuit. The Order's horse came back to the fight. The camp, the guns and the wagons were lost."
msgstr "The panic reached the camp. Zinnenberg's captor fell, and Zinnenberg himself was free again and led the pursuit. The Order's horse came back to the fight. The camp, the guns and the wagons were lost."

msgid "The patrol has raised the alarm"
msgstr "The patrol has raised the alarm"

msgid "The patrol has seen us! They are riding off to Orsha!"
msgstr "The patrol has seen us! They are riding off to Orsha!"

msgid "The peace was signed in Toruń, in the Artus Court, on 19 October 1466. It had been bargained over since 23 September at Nieszawa, with the papal legate Rudolf of Rüdesheim as go-between. Gdańsk Pomerania, the Chełmno land, Malbork, Elbląg and Warmia went to the Crown. The rest of Prussia stayed with the Order, but as a fief of the Polish king: every new Grand Master was to swear homage to the king within half a year of his election, to be his prince and councillor and to help him in war. The Order bound itself to take the king's subjects into its brotherhood as well."
msgstr "The peace was signed in Toruń, in the Artus Court, on 19 October 1466. It had been bargained over since 23 September at Nieszawa, with the papal legate Rudolf of Rüdesheim as go-between. Gdańsk Pomerania, the Chełmno land, Malbork, Elbląg and Warmia went to the Crown. The rest of Prussia stayed with the Order, but as a fief of the Polish king: every new Grand Master was to swear homage to the king within half a year of his election, to be his prince and councillor and to help him in war. The Order bound itself to take the king's subjects into its brotherhood as well."

msgid "The peasants throw down their scythes and run back into the forest. Long afterwards, it is told, drowned men were found in the lake there; nobody counted them."
msgstr "The peasants throw down their scythes and run back into the forest. Long afterwards, it is told, drowned men were found in the lake there; nobody counted them."

msgid "The pier is ours. No more boats will come to Skirsnemune."
msgstr "The pier is ours. No more boats will come to Skirsnemune."

msgid "The pier on the Nogat. Chests are carried into a long boat. A young Czech in a costly doublet counts them and laughs."
msgstr "The pier on the Nogat. Chests are carried into a long boat. A young Czech in a costly doublet counts them and laughs."

msgid "The piles of the old bridge lie in the Nogat above the castle. A boat that passes them without a tower on the bank to show the way strikes them."
msgstr "The piles of the old bridge lie in the Nogat above the castle. A boat that passes them without a tower on the bank to show the way strikes them."

msgid "The place is taken"
msgstr "The place is taken"

msgid "The plague grows with the crowding, the heat and with men standing on the canal below the town. A priest and an infirmary bring it down, but never to nothing. When it is high your healers do not heal and the men waste away."
msgstr "The plague grows with the crowding, the heat and with men standing on the canal below the town. A priest and an infirmary bring it down, but never to nothing. When it is high your healers do not heal and the men waste away."

msgid "The plague in the camp reaches its limit"
msgstr "The plague in the camp reaches its limit"

msgid "The port after «:» must be a number from 1 to 65535"
msgstr "The port after «:» must be a number from 1 to 65535"

msgid "The price is for each cell of the line."
msgstr "The price is for each cell of the line."

msgid "The priest can set up a chapel on a place of power now, while the day lasts: the cross on the road to Tuchola, the little chapel by the lake, the old oak at the edge of the bog."
msgstr "The priest can set up a chapel on a place of power now, while the day lasts: the cross on the road to Tuchola, the little chapel by the lake, the old oak at the edge of the bog."

msgid "The priest can set up a wayside cross on a place of power. Each cross gives Power for «Bogurodzica»."
msgstr "The priest can set up a wayside cross on a place of power. Each cross gives Power for «Bogurodzica»."

msgid "The priest can set up chapels: the wayside cross at Świecino, the little chapel on the lake shore, the boulder at the ford."
msgstr "The priest can set up chapels: the wayside cross at Świecino, the little chapel on the lake shore, the boulder at the ford."

msgid "The prince is gone! Bring the dogs! And tell the voivode: if we do not find him, they will ask it of us as of traitors."
msgstr "The prince is gone! Bring the dogs! And tell the voivode: if we do not find him, they will ask it of us as of traitors."

msgid "The prince says: he has seen. And that we are to hold the right edge."
msgstr "The prince says: he has seen. And that we are to hold the right edge."

msgid "The prince's. Prince Vytautas has not sent us yet. But the Germans held back the king's grain, and now the prince says he did not send us far enough."
msgstr "The prince's. Prince Vytautas has not sent us yet. But the Germans held back the king's grain, and now the prince says he did not send us far enough."

msgid "The prototype map: the forests and bogs of the Grand Duchy against the river and roads of the Order, a grove in the middle."
msgstr "The prototype map: the forests and bogs of the Grand Duchy against the river and roads of the Order, a grove in the middle."

msgid "The pursuers have lost their order. Turn on them now: a turn right after a retreat strikes hard."
msgstr "The pursuers have lost their order. Turn on them now: a turn right after a retreat strikes hard."

msgid "The queue is full"
msgstr "The queue is full"

msgid "The ransom for the guest knight you took at Grunwald has been paid: 100 silver."
msgstr "The ransom for the guest knight you took at Grunwald has been paid: 100 silver."

msgid "The rebels break camp in %s"
msgstr "The rebels break camp in %s"

msgid "The rebels come in %s"
msgstr "The rebels come in %s"

msgid "The rebels have gone. Slutsk has held."
msgstr "The rebels have gone. Slutsk has held."

msgid "The rebels have taken the Upper castle."
msgstr "The rebels have taken the Upper castle."

msgid "The rest you will take in Tczew."
msgstr "The rest you will take in Tczew."

msgid "The river is wicked here, pan Hynek. The old bridge stands under the water, I am from here, I know."
msgstr "The river is wicked here, pan Hynek. The old bridge stands under the water, I am from here, I know."

msgid "The road through the grove is boggy. Let us go over the hills, my lord."
msgstr "The road through the grove is boggy. Let us go over the hills, my lord."

msgid "The road to Sztum. A column of wagons with bombards in the dust. Jaśko rides at the tail and looks back at the castle."
msgstr "The road to Sztum. A column of wagons with bombards in the dust. Jaśko rides at the tail and looks back at the castle."

msgid "The round tower. A piece of masonry crashes down from above. When the dust settles a knight sits on the ground, alive, but his helmet is crushed flat. They lead him to the field forge. The smith takes aim with his hammer."
msgstr "The round tower. A piece of masonry crashes down from above. When the dust settles a knight sits on the ground, alive, but his helmet is crushed flat. They lead him to the field forge. The smith takes aim with his hammer."

msgid "The royal council did refuse to bribe the Czechs, calling it unknightly. Who first put the thought forward was not written down. Pan Jan said his great-grandfather did, and that the one in red had prompted him. Forty-seven years later the Crown will buy Malbork from Czech hirelings after all, and it will cost a hundred and ninety thousand florins."
msgstr "The royal council did refuse to bribe the Czechs, calling it unknightly. Who first put the thought forward was not written down. Pan Jan said his great-grandfather did, and that the one in red had prompted him. Forty-seven years later the Crown will buy Malbork from Czech hirelings after all, and it will cost a hundred and ninety thousand florins."

msgid "The same your grandfather paid."
msgstr "The same your grandfather paid."

msgid "The second Mass. If the Germans roast in their pots before noon, there will be nobody left for us to fight."
msgstr "The second Mass. If the Germans roast in their pots before noon, there will be nobody left for us to fight."

msgid "The second night. At dawn Švitrigaila's army will move."
msgstr "The second night. At dawn Švitrigaila's army will move."

msgid "The secret passage starts by the court in the Upper castle and comes out on the river bank to the north. Every workshop burned puts the next assault off by a minute. Order your men to set a workshop on fire, then come back."
msgstr "The secret passage starts by the court in the Upper castle and comes out on the river bank to the north. Every workshop burned puts the next assault off by a minute. Order your men to set a workshop on fire, then come back."

msgid "The shaft is pinned down by a dead horse. Jaśko jumps from the saddle and pulls; it will not come. Beside him a hand in a red sleeve takes hold of the shaft. A man without armour, in a red kaftan, with merry eyes. The fight seems to flow around him."
msgstr "The shaft is pinned down by a dead horse. Jaśko jumps from the saddle and pulls; it will not come. Beside him a hand in a red sleeve takes hold of the shaft. A man without armour, in a red kaftan, with merry eyes. The fight seems to flow around him."

msgid "The siege is lifted, and the guns have come to Sztum."
msgstr "The siege is lifted, and the guns have come to Sztum."

msgid "The silver is handed over. Every load raises the mercenaries' patience."
msgstr "The silver is handed over. Every load raises the mercenaries' patience."

msgid "The square of Tczew. The knechts and hirelings of the Order who gave themselves up kneel. Some of them speak Czech. From afar the orphans come with torches and a tar barrel."
msgstr "The square of Tczew. The knechts and hirelings of the Order who gave themselves up kneel. Some of them speak Czech. From afar the orphans come with torches and a tar barrel."

msgid "The sun goes down to the west, the shadows grow long. Moscow brings fresh men into the field again and again."
msgstr "The sun goes down to the west, the shadows grow long. Moscow brings fresh men into the field again and again."

msgid "The town is ours. A battery by St John's church stands under cover of its stone: the castle's balls do it less harm."
msgstr "The town is ours. A battery by St John's church stands under cover of its stone: the castle's balls do it less harm."

msgid "The townsmen come out against the hill. The villages round about still have food and silver: whoever comes first takes it. The orphans do not wait, and what they plunder they burn."
msgstr "The townsmen come out against the hill. The villages round about still have food and silver: whoever comes first takes it. The orphans do not wait, and what they plunder they burn."

msgid "The truth. That we were baptized. That for years the Germans burned our yards and took our people. That we want the cross, but not the German cross."
msgstr "The truth. That we were baptized. That for years the Germans burned our yards and took our people. That we want the cross, but not the German cross."

msgid "The two games have drifted apart at %s. Replay saved: %s"
msgstr "The two games have drifted apart at %s. Replay saved: %s"

msgid "The village burns down"
msgstr "The village burns down"

msgid "The village has burned down."
msgstr "The village has burned down."

msgid "The village ran out of food and starved."
msgstr "The village ran out of food and starved."

msgid "The wagon fort! Strike the wagon fort before they come to their senses!"
msgstr "The wagon fort! Strike the wagon fort before they come to their senses!"

msgid "The wagons are chained and the ditch is dug. The enemy cannot break the chained wagons, and his horse loses its run-up in the ditch."
msgstr "The wagons are chained and the ditch is dug. The enemy cannot break the chained wagons, and his horse loses its run-up in the ditch."

msgid "The wagons are empty: without food Jaśko's men lose heart. Take food from the villages before the orphans do."
msgstr "The wagons are empty: without food Jaśko's men lose heart. Take food from the villages before the orphans do."

msgid "The wagons bring food, wood, iron and silver to the field camp every minute. Camp servants can put up a stable, an archery range and an alka; hire light horse and archers there."
msgstr "The wagons bring food, wood, iron and silver to the field camp every minute. Camp servants can put up a stable, an archery range and an alka; hire light horse and archers there."

msgid "The wagons first, Fritz. The Poles have learned from the Czechs, and it is no sin for us to."
msgstr "The wagons first, Fritz. The Poles have learned from the Czechs, and it is no sin for us to."

msgid "The watch sees in a cone the way it faces: half as far at night, further with a torch, twice as far into a campfire's light. Their dogs smell whoever comes near, and a trot is heard even behind their backs. Keep to the forest: the prince is not seen there at all, his servants only close up."
msgstr "The watch sees in a cone the way it faces: half as far at night, further with a torch, twice as far into a campfire's light. Their dogs smell whoever comes near, and a trot is heard even behind their backs. Keep to the forest: the prince is not seen there at all, his servants only close up."

msgid "The wind blows from the west, towards the wall. Order men to set fire to the westmost houses of the suburb: the fire runs east from house to house, and when the suburb has burned down it takes the town gate. Keep your men out of the smoke east of a fire: it burns whoever stands downwind."
msgstr "The wind blows from the west, towards the wall. Order men to set fire to the westmost houses of the suburb: the fire runs east from house to house, and when the suburb has burned down it takes the town gate. Keep your men out of the smoke east of a fire: it burns whoever stands downwind."

msgid "The znakharka can call Bog Mist: your units in it cannot be seen until they attack."
msgstr "The znakharka can call Bog Mist: your units in it cannot be seen until they attack."

msgid "The «Concord» bar shows how Mikołaj and Čapek stand with each other. Unpaid wages, killed prisoners and quarrels lower it. At zero the orphans stop listening to the common order for a while; twice, and they go home."
msgstr "The «Concord» bar shows how Mikołaj and Čapek stand with each other. Unpaid wages, killed prisoners and quarrels lower it. At zero the orphans stop listening to the common order for a while; twice, and they go home."

msgid "The «Siege» bar is not the damage to the walls but the hunger in the castle. The garrison mends the walls every night; only time and the shot starve them."
msgstr "The «Siege» bar is not the damage to the walls but the hunger in the castle. The garrison mends the walls every night; only time and the shot starve them."

msgid "The Łęczyca banner is in the enemy's hands."
msgstr "The Łęczyca banner is in the enemy's hands."

msgid "The Łęczyca banner is taken by the enemy"
msgstr "The Łęczyca banner is taken by the enemy"

msgid "The Łęczyca horsemen strain after those running to the walls. Stach turns his horse. Jaśko seizes its bridle."
msgstr "The Łęczyca horsemen strain after those running to the walls. Stach turns his horse. Jaśko seizes its bridle."

msgid "The Łęczyca place in the line is in the middle of the field, north of the camp. The clock on the right shows the hour: the king gives the signal in the evening."
msgstr "The Łęczyca place in the line is in the middle of the field, north of the camp. The clock on the right shows the hour: the king gives the signal in the evening."

msgid "The Żuławy between Gdańsk and Malbork, the Vistula and the Nogat. From August 1456 to June 1457."
msgstr "The Żuławy between Gdańsk and Malbork, the Vistula and the Nogat. From August 1456 to June 1457."

msgid "Then click your building."
msgstr "Then click your building."

msgid "Then do not ask where my men find their pay."
msgstr "Then do not ask where my men find their pay."

msgid "Then men who know how to retreat. You will not need that skill here. We have nowhere to retreat to."
msgstr "Then men who know how to retreat. You will not need that skill here. We have nowhere to retreat to."

msgid "Then the castle must stand until tomorrow, mother."
msgstr "Then the castle must stand until tomorrow, mother."

msgid "Then the prince and I take the head, and you the middle. And mind, lord, in the middle ride the Ruthenian banners. Won't your hand shake?"
msgstr "Then the prince and I take the head, and you the middle. And mind, lord, in the middle ride the Ruthenian banners. Won't your hand shake?"

msgid "Then two heralds came from the Master and brought two swords. On one shield was the black eagle of the King of the Romans, on the other the griffin of Szczecin. They said: here are swords for you, if your own are too few, and choose the field, if you are afraid."
msgstr "Then two heralds came from the Master and brought two swords. On one shield was the black eagle of the King of the Romans, on the other the griffin of Szczecin. They said: here are swords for you, if your own are too few, and choose the field, if you are afraid."

msgid "Then we will pray quickly."
msgstr "Then we will pray quickly."

msgid "There are fewer of them, Kaspar. Let us strike at once."
msgstr "There are fewer of them, Kaspar. Let us strike at once."

msgid "There are fish in the lake and honey in the hives. The Germans cannot search the whole forest."
msgstr "There are fish in the lake and honey in the hives. The Germans cannot search the whole forest."

msgid "There is a ford lower down, I watered my horse there! Two at a time, not in a crowd! Whoever goes in all at once will drown."
msgstr "There is a ford lower down, I watered my horse there! Two at a time, not in a crowd! Whoever goes in all at once will drown."

msgid "There is not enough silver in the company's chest."
msgstr "There is not enough silver in the company's chest."

msgid "There is not silver enough in the chest. Čapek counts it as a refusal."
msgstr "There is not silver enough in the chest. Čapek counts it as a refusal."

msgid "There is the other way. After me, to the tent!"
msgstr "There is the other way. After me, to the tent!"

msgid "There is the sign! All their elders are sitting there now, under one pillar!"
msgstr "There is the sign! All their elders are sitting there now, under one pillar!"

msgid "There they are! How many of them…"
msgstr "There they are! How many of them…"

msgid "There they go, running. Time we went too."
msgstr "There they go, running. Time we went too."

msgid "There was not silver enough for the pay: the companies nobody could pay have left the field."
msgstr "There was not silver enough for the pay: the companies nobody could pay have left the field."

msgid "There was nothing to pay the hired men with, and some of them have left. A horseman asks 200 florins a month, a foot soldier 100."
msgstr "There was nothing to pay the hired men with, and some of them have left. A horseman asks 200 florins a month, a foot soldier 100."

msgid "These Czechs sold their faith to the Germans. We have our own account with them."
msgstr "These Czechs sold their faith to the Germans. We have our own account with them."

msgid "These are no knechts! Who are they?"
msgstr "These are no knechts! Who are they?"

msgid "They are leaving. They did not even take the ladders."
msgstr "They are leaving. They did not even take the ladders."

msgid "They are not running. They are leaving. See how evenly? Hold the line!"
msgstr "They are not running. They are leaving. See how evenly? Hold the line!"

msgid "They are tying up the wagons and putting out the fires early. They are leaving for Vilkomir."
msgstr "They are tying up the wagons and putting out the fires early. They are leaving for Vilkomir."

msgid "They are watching their own bridges, at Orsha. And we are building ours."
msgstr "They are watching their own bridges, at Orsha. And we are building ours."

msgid "They brought these for us. They knew how it would end."
msgstr "They brought these for us. They knew how it would end."

msgid "They cut down the old oak."
msgstr "They cut down the old oak."

msgid "They did not know. They thought they knew."
msgstr "They did not know. They thought they knew."

msgid "They have an icon, and we have an icon. Whom will God help, then?"
msgstr "They have an icon, and we have an icon. Whom will God help, then?"

msgid "They have been coughing for a whole week. Did you do this to them?"
msgstr "They have been coughing for a whole week. Did you do this to them?"

msgid "They have long been waiting for it, prince."
msgstr "They have long been waiting for it, prince."

msgid "They have. We go on. For now."
msgstr "They have. We go on. For now."

msgid "They know three. The middle one leads straight to their wagons."
msgstr "They know three. The middle one leads straight to their wagons."

msgid "They met at a lake near Vilkomir and stood. And my grandfather Mikołaj stood on the east shore and counted the fires on the west. He hoped his brother was not sitting at one of them."
msgstr "They met at a lake near Vilkomir and stood. And my grandfather Mikołaj stood on the east shore and counted the fires on the west. He hoped his brother was not sitting at one of them."

msgid "They run! Moscow runs!"
msgstr "They run! Moscow runs!"

msgid "They say a thunderstorm passed over the field in that hour, and lightning struck where the Germans stood. They say. I would like to believe it."
msgstr "They say a thunderstorm passed over the field in that hour, and lightning struck where the Germans stood. They say. I would like to believe it."

msgid "They say old Gintaut laughed when he was asked whether the Lithuanians ran at Grunwald. Now I understand why. Sound the retreat!"
msgstr "They say old Gintaut laughed when he was asked whether the Lithuanians ran at Grunwald. Now I understand why. Sound the retreat!"

msgid "They say that in the Summer Refectory the Germans held council under one pillar, and a traitor hung a red cap in the window, and ours fired at the pillar and missed. The ball in the wall above the fireplace is shown to this day. But everyone tells it his own way, and that only happens with tales. And Jaśko, pan Jan said, stood a long time after that shot looking at what red thing had been in that window."
msgstr "They say that in the Summer Refectory the Germans held council under one pillar, and a traitor hung a red cap in the window, and ours fired at the pillar and missed. The ball in the wall above the fireplace is shown to this day. But everyone tells it his own way, and that only happens with tales. And Jaśko, pan Jan said, stood a long time after that shot looking at what red thing had been in that window."

msgid "They say the mist rose from the bog in broad daylight, and a German patrol passed ten steps from our men and saw no one. Such mists do happen in Samogitia. But grandfather said that one was special."
msgstr "They say the mist rose from the bog in broad daylight, and a German patrol passed ten steps from our men and saw no one. Such mists do happen in Samogitia. But grandfather said that one was special."

msgid "They say there are three times fewer Germans. It will all be over by dinner."
msgstr "They say there are three times fewer Germans. It will all be over by dinner."

msgid "They sing the same as we do, lord standard-bearer."
msgstr "They sing the same as we do, lord standard-bearer."

msgid "They sing the same. But they came for something else."
msgstr "They sing the same. But they came for something else."

msgid "They took forty-two princes captive. They took Prince Sigismund Korybutovich too, who had fought alongside the Czech heretics, and he soon died. Of what he died they write differently, and I will not choose."
msgstr "They took forty-two princes captive. They took Prince Sigismund Korybutovich too, who had fought alongside the Czech heretics, and he soon died. Of what he died they write differently, and I will not choose."

msgid "They took the bread, now the grove. Take up your spears."
msgstr "They took the bread, now the grove. Take up your spears."

msgid "They will come again, and all together. Let our horse give way before them. Not run, but give way: straight under the Gdańsk crossbows. Pan Stach, this is yours. Can you retreat so that they follow you?"
msgstr "They will come again, and all together. Let our horse give way before them. Not run, but give way: straight under the Gdańsk crossbows. Pan Stach, this is yours. Can you retreat so that they follow you?"

msgid "They will not ask about the grove. And if they ask, say that we have plenty of firewood."
msgstr "They will not ask about the grove. And if they ask, say that we have plenty of firewood."

msgid "They will take the land anyway."
msgstr "They will take the land anyway."

msgid "This I saw myself. Thunder without lightning, as a Samogitian once said at Grunwald. Only now the powder was dry, and the guns were ours."
msgstr "This I saw myself. Thunder without lightning, as a Samogitian once said at Grunwald. Only now the powder was dry, and the guns were ours."

msgid "This is the interest. Sea water is dear at home: nobody drinks it and nobody pours it out. A debt stays a debt."
msgstr "This is the interest. Sea water is dear at home: nobody drinks it and nobody pours it out. A debt stays a debt."

msgid "This time you found it yourself, prince."
msgstr "This time you found it yourself, prince."

msgid "This too Długosz wrote down. They knocked the helmet off with hammers, and pan Piotr lived."
msgstr "This too Długosz wrote down. They knocked the helmet off with hammers, and pan Piotr lived."

msgid "Three years after the great battle King Jogaila and Grand Duke Vytautas came to Samogitia to baptize it, and Gintaut was among the first to step into the river. Now the Order says that the Samogitians are baptized in name only, and its spies are gathering evidence for the council at Konstanz."
msgstr "Three years after the great battle King Jogaila and Grand Duke Vytautas came to Samogitia to baptize it, and Gintaut was among the first to step into the river. Now the Order says that the Samogitians are baptized in name only, and its spies are gathering evidence for the council at Konstanz."

msgid "Three years after the great battle, King Jogaila and Grand Duke Vytautas came to Samogitia themselves. Długosz writes that they cut down the groves and put out the fires. Great-grandfather did not tell it so. He said that it was cold, and that the king spoke to the people in our tongue."
msgstr "Three years after the great battle, King Jogaila and Grand Duke Vytautas came to Samogitia themselves. Długosz writes that they cut down the groves and put out the fires. Great-grandfather did not tell it so. He said that it was cold, and that the king spoke to the people in our tongue."

msgid "Throw back the blow of the Order's right wing"
msgstr "Throw back the blow of the Order's right wing"

msgid "Thunder without lightning!"
msgstr "Thunder without lightning!"

msgid "Time: %d s"
msgstr "Time: %d s"

msgid "Tired"
msgstr "Tired"

msgid "To horse! We go at the signal, not before. Whoever jumps out first for glory, the Germans will take first."
msgstr "To horse! We go at the signal, not before. Whoever jumps out first for glory, the Germans will take first."

msgid "To the bridge! Everyone to the bridge!"
msgstr "To the bridge! Everyone to the bridge!"

msgid "To the sea. The shore at Oliwa is north-west of the hill."
msgstr "To the sea. The shore at Oliwa is north-west of the hill."

msgid "To the wagons! Shooters into the gaps!"
msgstr "To the wagons! Shooters into the gaps!"

msgid "To the wagons! Strike their wagenburg before they come to their senses!"
msgstr "To the wagons! Strike their wagenburg before they come to their senses!"

msgid "To win, destroy the enemy's capital, or hold every place of power for 5 minutes."
msgstr "To win, destroy the enemy's capital, or hold every place of power for 5 minutes."

msgid "Towers, walls and gates see 2 cells farther."
msgstr "Towers, walls and gates see 2 cells farther."

msgid "Towns sworn: %d"
msgstr "Towns sworn: %d"

msgid "Trains archers and crossbowmen."
msgstr "Trains archers and crossbowmen."

msgid "Trains foot soldiers."
msgstr "Trains foot soldiers."

msgid "Trains horsemen."
msgstr "Trains horsemen."

msgid "Trains: %s"
msgstr "Trains: %s"

msgid "Treasury: %s florins"
msgstr "Treasury: %s florins"

msgid "Trophy wagons from Tczew and two banners of Czech hirelings from its garrison have come over to Jaśko."
msgstr "Trophy wagons from Tczew and two banners of Czech hirelings from its garrison have come over to Jaśko."

msgid "Turn and face the chasers at once."
msgstr "Turn and face the chasers at once."

msgid "Turn around"
msgstr "Turn around"

msgid "Twenty-five thousand! The captain will be pleased. I will take it to the castle, pani, and you go for the rest."
msgstr "Twenty-five thousand! The captain will be pleased. I will take it to the castle, pani, and you go for the rest."

msgid "Twenty-three years, pan Jaśko. You have gone grey, and I have not. Pour one for me too."
msgstr "Twenty-three years, pan Jaśko. You have gone grey, and I have not. Pour one for me too."

msgid "Twilight. Bniński without his helmet, his face bloody, fights by his banner. They surround him. A horseman in the Order's white cloak shouts something to him. Bniński throws his sword at his feet."
msgstr "Twilight. Bniński without his helmet, his face bloody, fights by his banner. They surround him. A horseman in the Order's white cloak shouts something to him. Bniński throws his sword at his feet."

msgid "Two armies face each other. Over both of them icons. On both sides they sing the same words."
msgstr "Two armies face each other. Over both of them icons. On both sides they sing the same words."

msgid "Two fresh Lithuanian banners have gathered at the forest. The reserve is going for the Poles: strike it in the flank before it breaks through. The znakharka can call Perkūnas's Wrath on it."
msgstr "Two fresh Lithuanian banners have gathered at the forest. The reserve is going for the Poles: strike it in the flank before it breaks through. The znakharka can call Perkūnas's Wrath on it."

msgid "Two years after Chojnice pan Jan, not yet born then, might have been left without a father: Stach was sent to Malbork with a letter to the mercenaries, and not everyone came back from Malbork in those days. The Order did not pay its mercenaries, and they looked for money wherever they could, even in the bed of the Grand Master himself."
msgstr "Two years after Chojnice pan Jan, not yet born then, might have been left without a father: Stach was sent to Malbork with a letter to the mercenaries, and not everyone came back from Malbork in those days. The Order did not pay its mercenaries, and they looked for money wherever they could, even in the bed of the Grand Master himself."

msgid "Two years after Chojnice the Order has no money to pay its mercenaries. The Bohemian captain Červenka holds Malbork, the Order's capital, and is ready to sell it to the Crown, if only the Crown pays. The money has to be borrowed in Gdańsk and carried across the Żuławy. Stach has gone to the mercenaries with the king's letter; the silver is the business of his elder sister Barbara, Jaśko's granddaughter and a Gdańsk merchant's wife."
msgstr "Two years after Chojnice the Order has no money to pay its mercenaries. The Bohemian captain Červenka holds Malbork, the Order's capital, and is ready to sell it to the Crown, if only the Crown pays. The money has to be borrowed in Gdańsk and carried across the Żuławy. Stach has gone to the mercenaries with the king's letter; the silver is the business of his elder sister Barbara, Jaśko's granddaughter and a Gdańsk merchant's wife."

msgid "Type the host's address"
msgstr "Type the host's address"

msgid "Under construction: %d%%"
msgstr "Under construction: %d%%"

msgid "Units killed"
msgstr "Units killed"

msgid "Units lost"
msgstr "Units lost"

msgid "Units trained"
msgstr "Units trained"

msgid "Units walk over it"
msgstr "Units walk over it"

msgid "Units with the speech mark argue over their place and do not move. Ride up to your arguing men with Jaśko or Stach and they will go. The rest of the army will take its time."
msgstr "Units with the speech mark argue over their place and do not move. Ride up to your arguing men with Jaśko or Stach and they will go. The rest of the army will take its time."

msgid "Unseen in the forest until it shoots"
msgstr "Unseen in the forest until it shoots"

msgid "Vedrosha"
msgstr "Vedrosha"

msgid "Version %s"
msgstr "Version %s"

msgid "Very fast"
msgstr "Very fast"

msgid "Very large"
msgstr "Very large"

msgid "Victory"
msgstr "Victory"

msgid "Villages: %d ours, %d plundered"
msgstr "Villages: %d ours, %d plundered"

msgid "Vilnius, in the 1520s. A room full of books. Old Maciej is writing the last page."
msgstr "Vilnius, in the 1520s. A room full of books. Old Maciej is writing the last page."

msgid "Voices"
msgstr "Voices"

msgid "W A S D, the arrows or the screen edge move the view."
msgstr "W A S D, the arrows or the screen edge move the view."

msgid "Wages each month: %s florins"
msgstr "Wages each month: %s florins"

msgid "Wagons in a ring, wheels on the chain, a ditch two spades deep. Left side to the little lake. The Czechs once beat us like this; now we shall beat them like this."
msgstr "Wagons in a ring, wheels on the chain, a ditch two spades deep. Left side to the little lake. The Czechs once beat us like this; now we shall beat them like this."

msgid "Wagons: %d"
msgstr "Wagons: %d"

msgid "Wait for the order and do not ride out before it"
msgstr "Wait for the order and do not ride out before it"

msgid "Wait for the order, then hold the blow of the Order's right wing. When the great banner of the kingdom falls, raise it. Do not let the Grand Master's reserve reach the king, and take the wagenburg together with the Lithuanians."
msgstr "Wait for the order, then hold the blow of the Order's right wing. When the great banner of the kingdom falls, raise it. Do not let the Grand Master's reserve reach the king, and take the wagenburg together with the Lithuanians."

msgid "Wait out the day and reach the border ford"
msgstr "Wait out the day and reach the border ford"

msgid "Waiting for the other player. Your address: %s"
msgstr "Waiting for the other player. Your address: %s"

msgid "Waiting for the other player…"
msgstr "Waiting for the other player…"

msgid "Walk and stand in a broad line."
msgstr "Walk and stand in a broad line."

msgid "Walk in a narrow column, for roads and the forest."
msgstr "Walk in a narrow column, for roads and the forest."

msgid "War, prince. Prince Glinski has quarrelled with the lords, and they say no good will come of it."
msgstr "War, prince. Prince Glinski has quarrelled with the lords, and they say no good will come of it."

msgid "Water in bottles. And a truce. The Order has understood that we can come to the sea and go back."
msgstr "Water in bottles. And a truce. The Order has understood that we can come to the sea and go back."

msgid "Wavering"
msgstr "Wavering"

msgid "We are at the wall already! Another hundred paces!"
msgstr "We are at the wall already! Another hundred paces!"

msgid "We are going on to Malbork now. I need your men in Samogitia. Go home."
msgstr "We are going on to Malbork now. I need your men in Samogitia. Go home."

msgid "We could buy the gate. The Czechs in the garrison can be bought, knowing men say."
msgstr "We could buy the gate. The Czechs in the garrison can be bought, knowing men say."

msgid "We could. But at Grunwald we took the field by the sword. Buying a castle from hirelings is no knightly deed."
msgstr "We could. But at Grunwald we took the field by the sword. Buying a castle from hirelings is no knightly deed."

msgid "We did not take Chojnice, we did not take Gdańsk, we burned Tczew. What are we taking home, pan Mikołaj?"
msgstr "We did not take Chojnice, we did not take Gdańsk, we burned Tczew. What are we taking home, pan Mikołaj?"

msgid "We had to wait a long time for peace. But grandfather told how great-grandfather that evening, for the first time in his life, fell asleep without fear."
msgstr "We had to wait a long time for peace. But grandfather told how great-grandfather that evening, for the first time in his life, fell asleep without fear."

msgid "We have swords enough. But this one I will take, and let God be the judge. Nor will we look for a field: such as the Lord has sent us, on that we shall stand."
msgstr "We have swords enough. But this one I will take, and let God be the judge. Nor will we look for a field: such as the Lord has sent us, on that we shall stand."

msgid "We have swords enough. Gintaut! Your Samogitians will be the first to hear the trumpet."
msgstr "We have swords enough. Gintaut! Your Samogitians will be the first to hear the trumpet."

msgid "We lift the siege. We take the guns with us, not one shall we leave them. We go to Sztum and put our own men there."
msgstr "We lift the siege. We take the guns with us, not one shall we leave them. We go to Sztum and put our own men there."

msgid "We lit it. Others stacked the firewood."
msgstr "We lit it. Others stacked the firewood."

msgid "We never had to storm Dubysa. Vogt Michael set fire to his own castle so that we would not have it, and led his sick men away to Prussia. The Germans wrote of sickness. But in the Samogitian villages they said otherwise."
msgstr "We never had to storm Dubysa. Vogt Michael set fire to his own castle so that we would not have it, and led his sick men away to Prussia. The Germans wrote of sickness. But in the Samogitian villages they said otherwise."

msgid "Wedge"
msgstr "Wedge"

msgid "Well said. But it would be better if you brought them something besides words."
msgstr "Well said. But it would be better if you brought them something besides words."

msgid "Well, Jan? Have your men had their fill of standing about?"
msgstr "Well, Jan? Have your men had their fill of standing about?"

msgid "What I need is for the crossbowmen not to oversleep in the morning. That I will see to myself. Go your way, pan. You are in the candle's light."
msgstr "What I need is for the crossbowmen not to oversleep in the morning. That I will see to myself. Go your way, pan. You are in the candle's light."

msgid "What are we to say there, before the holy fathers?"
msgstr "What are we to say there, before the holy fathers?"

msgid "What do I pay, mother?"
msgstr "What do I pay, mother?"

msgid "What will Gintaut do with the oak?"
msgstr "What will Gintaut do with the oak?"

msgid "What will Gintaut offer the pagans for peace?"
msgstr "What will Gintaut offer the pagans for peace?"

msgid "Where is the nearest German castle?"
msgstr "Where is the nearest German castle?"

msgid "Where it stands"
msgstr "Where it stands"

msgid "Which banner kneels next?"
msgstr "Which banner kneels next?"

msgid "While they argue, the sun goes down. Stach, set our men out, do not wait for an order."
msgstr "While they argue, the sun goes down. Stach, set our men out, do not wait for an order."

msgid "Who will be the first to step into the water?"
msgstr "Who will be the first to step into the water?"

msgid "Whoever stands longer."
msgstr "Whoever stands longer."

msgid "Whose banner?"
msgstr "Whose banner?"

msgid "Wild, nobody's"
msgstr "Wild, nobody's"

msgid "Wind: from the west"
msgstr "Wind: from the west"

msgid "Winter 1456–1457"
msgstr "Winter 1456–1457"

msgid "Winter. The canals and the rivers of the Żuławy freeze. Sledges go straight across the fields, and the Order's riders cross the ice wherever they like."
msgstr "Winter. The canals and the rivers of the Żuławy freeze. Sledges go straight across the fields, and the Order's riders cross the ice wherever they like."

msgid "Wise women heal 2 HP a second instead of 1."
msgstr "Wise women heal 2 HP a second instead of 1."

msgid "With God! Lances down, hold the line, do not scatter!"
msgstr "With God! Lances down, hold the line, do not scatter!"

msgid "With God. Gintovt, your ford."
msgstr "With God. Gintovt, your ford."

msgid "With peasants selected, the buttons at the bottom right are buildings."
msgstr "With peasants selected, the buttons at the bottom right are buildings."

msgid "With the Livonians came marshal Vincke, and he had few men. Vytautas met him beyond the Pasłęka, and they agreed on a truce for the northern lands, and the marshal himself was escorted into the castle to talk. Plauen got not an army but a hope."
msgstr "With the Livonians came marshal Vincke, and he had few men. Vytautas met him beyond the Pasłęka, and they agreed on a truce for the northern lands, and the marshal himself was escorted into the castle to talk. Plauen got not an army but a hope."

